window.GEAR_BOOK_CONTENTS["book-31"] = [{"id":7,"rawContent":"# 第七章：青銅雕像裡的肋骨\n\n雨幕中的濱江市現代藝術館，宛如一艘由純白大理石與幾何玻璃拼接而成的巨型幽靈旗艦，沉默地錨泊在雲濱高新區的江畔廣場中央。\n\n上午十點整，原本應該冠蓋雲集、名流穿梭的「當代解構主義人體藝術大展」中央穹頂展廳，此刻卻被刺目的黃黑警戒線重重封鎖。數十名荷槍實彈的防暴特警將所有受邀參觀的藝術評論家、收藏家與媒體記者隔絕在百米之外，空氣中瀰漫著高檔香水與刺鼻消毒水雜糅後的詭異氣息。\n\n「讓開讓開！局長特批現場勘驗，別擋著我們家首席法醫的清淨道！」\n\n老周那粗獷嘹亮的嗓門撕裂了展廳內沉重的死寂。他邁著大步穿過旋轉玻璃門，右手裡赫然端著一隻粉紅色、帶有電子螢幕的智慧型語音保溫杯——那是蘇棠今早看不下去他那隻大紅喜字鐵皮桶，自掏腰包給他買的「工傷慰問品」。\n\n「主人，現在水溫五十五度，已為您保溫兩小時，請注意及時補充水分哦！」保溫杯突然發出一聲甜美呆萌的電子女聲。\n\n老周老臉一抽，趕緊把杯蓋旋鈕擰死，乾咳兩聲掩飾尷尬，轉頭看向身側的裴以安：「小裴，我說這玩意兒能不能把語音關了？老子這輩子抓了幾百個殺人犯，今天差點被一個杯子整神經衰弱。」\n\n裴以安並未理會老周的自嘲。他穿著一身纖塵不染的黑色長風衣，戴著全新的淺藍色丁腈無菌手套，目光越過大理石地面上的警戒線，筆直投向展廳正中央那座高達三米半的巨型青銅雕像。\n\n雕像的名字叫《被剝皮的普羅米修斯》，由濱江市旅歐先鋒雕塑大師嚴克己歷時三年創作，原本預定在今天的開幕式上作為壓軸之作進行全球揭幕。\n\n那是一尊充滿力量感與殘酷美學的現代青銅人像，軀幹表面的金屬被故意拉扯、撕裂成肌肉纖維的鏤空紋理。然而，就在二十分鐘前，館方工作人員進行燈光除塵時，聚光燈的高溫烘烤使得青銅胸腔深處滲出了一滴粘稠發黑的液體，伴隨著一股濃烈的福馬林與骨膠腥臭。\n\n當工作人員驚恐地用強光手電照向鏤空的胸腔內部時，映入眼簾的景象讓現場所有人當場失聲尖叫——\n\n在那繁複精巧的青銅肌肉紋理下方，包裹著一副真實、完整且慘白的人體骨骼！\n\n「嚴大師人呢？」老周收斂了玩笑神色，眼神如鷹隼般掃向四周。\n\n「在隔壁貴賓室，已經嚇得心律失常吞了兩顆速效救心丸。」早先一步趕到現場的蘇棠小跑過來，手裡抱著光譜物證勘查箱，臉色蒼白，「嚴克己聲稱這尊雕像是他在城郊的私人工作室完成鑄造的，但泥塑翻模與青銅熔鑄的中空內膽是由一家外包金屬工藝廠代工，他根本不知道裡面被塞進了真人骸骨！」\n\n「泥塑翻模無法容納真實骨骼在高溫銅水中的熱膨脹係數。」裴以安踩著專用鞋套踏上展示台，冷靜的聲音清澈如水，「青銅熔點是一千零八十三度，在這種溫度下，人體骨骼中的羥基磷灰石晶體會崩解粉碎，有機膠原蛋白更是會瞬間碳化。這副骨骼，是在青銅外殼鑄造冷卻完成後，被人從雕像後背預留的精密檢修滑槽中，一片一片以解剖學手法精準拼裝植入進去的。」\n\n裴以安打開強光勘驗燈，將光束透過青銅肋骨的縫隙照入內部。\n\n只見在青銅普羅米修斯的胸腔深處，十二對肋骨排列得嚴絲合縫，每一處胸肋關節都用直徑零點二毫米的純銀外科絲線精心縫合，肋軟骨部分則被替換成了半透明的醫用矽膠固化劑，晶瑩剔透，宛如一座懸掛在金屬熔爐深處的象牙鐘乳石森林。\n\n「死者性別男性，年齡在二十五到二十八歲之間。」裴以安取出細長的純銀解剖鑷，探入青銅縫隙，輕輕刮取胸骨柄表面的一點微量殘留物，「骨面光滑無肉，無任何殘留軟組織腐敗氣味。這不是常規的自然白骨化，而是採用了法醫人類學實驗室級別的『皮蠹甲蟲生物噬咬法』，並輔以百分之三濃度的過氧化氫低溫漂白。」\n\n「你的意思是……兇手是個極其專業的解剖狂？」老周的眼神沉了下來。\n\n「不只是解剖狂，更是一個對人體骨骼結構有病態崇拜的偏執狂。」裴以安的指尖停留在死者第四根左側真肋的中央位置，「老周，手電光調到微距聚焦，看這裡。」\n\n老周湊上前去，透過手電筒的高倍偏振光片，他倒吸了一口涼氣。\n\n只見那根蒼白的第四肋骨骨幹外側，被人用極其細微的激光微雕技術，密密麻麻地刻下了一行微型五線譜！\n\n五線譜的開頭是一個低音譜號，後面緊跟著四個音符：**D - E - A - D**。\n\n而在五線譜的最右側，刻著一個極小的金屬齒輪印記，以及一行縮寫：\n\n**「Op. 02：獻給骨骼交響曲的第二小提琴手。」**\n\n「DEAD……死者。」老周喃喃自語，嘴唇緊繃，「第二樂章真的來了……擺渡人沒在開玩笑，他在現代藝術館的青銅雕像裡，給咱們留了一具被做成樂譜的骨架！」\n\n就在這時，展廳門口傳來一陣急促沉重的皮鞋腳步聲。\n\n一名身材魁梧、面容剛毅的中年男子在一群便衣警員的簇擁下大步走入展廳。他穿著一身筆挺的二級警監制服，肩章上的警銜在無影燈下泛著冷硬的光芒，正是濱江市公安局新任常務副局長——陸天明。\n\n「周成林！裴以安！」陸天明的臉色陰沉得幾乎能滴出水來，人還未到，威嚴的低吼便在展廳穹頂下迴盪，「市委宣傳部和省廳的電話已經打爆了我的辦公室！今天這座藝術館裡有一百二十位境內外主流媒體的記者！四十八小時……省廳只給了我們四十八小時查明屍源破案！」\n\n老周挑了挑眉，漫不經心地抿了一口粉紅保溫杯裡的熱水：「陸副局長，別這麼大火氣嘛。我們家小裴剛看了一眼，連死者生前的骨齡、死因防腐手法都推出來了，您這四十八小時，我看足夠請兇手吃兩頓局裡的豬肉白菜水餃。」\n\n陸天明狠狠瞪了老周一眼，深吸一口氣，將目光轉向依舊專注凝視著青銅骨骼的裴以安：「裴顧問，死者生前到底是誰？有沒有身份特徵線索？」\n\n裴以安收回鑷子，取下手套，清澈的眼眸平靜地迎向陸天明那帶著審視與重壓的目光。\n\n「死者的胸骨劍突處有微小的向內凹陷變形，兩側鎖骨中外三分之一處骨皮質增厚，伴有陳舊性應力性骨質增生。」裴以安從隨身金屬盒裡彈出一顆薄荷糖扔進嘴裡，神色淡然地宣佈：\n\n「這不是普通人。死者長期將某種硬木樂器緊壓在左鎖骨與下頜骨之間，每天重複持弓施壓動作超過八小時。」\n\n裴以安轉過身，指著雕像胸腔裡那根刻著五線譜的第四肋骨：\n\n「死者是一名專業的小提琴演奏家。而且，他的失蹤時間，不會超過七天。」","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 7: Ribs Inside the Bronze Statue\n\nShrouded in sheets of rain, the Binjiang Museum of Modern Art resembled a colossal ghost flagship assembled of pure white marble and geometric glass, anchored silently in the center of the riverside plaza of the Yunbin Hi-Tech Zone.\n\nAt 10:00 a.m. sharp, the central rotunda of the \"Grand Exhibition of Contemporary Deconstructive Somatic Art\"—which should have been teeming with dignitaries and socialites—was cordoned off behind dense rows of glaring black-and-yellow police tape. Dozens of riot police armed with live ammunition held all invited art critics, collectors, and press correspondents at bay a hundred meters away, as a bizarre aroma mingling high-end perfume and pungent chemical disinfectant hung heavily in the air.\n\n\"Out of the way, make way! Bureau Chief special clearance on scene—don't block the corridor for our chief forensic pathologist!\"\n\nOld Zhou's boisterous, gravelly bellow shattered the oppressive silence inside the exhibition rotunda. Striding briskly through the revolving glass doors, he gripped in his right hand a bright pink smart voice-enabled thermos fitted with a glowing digital display—a \"compassionate workplace wellness gift\" Su Tang had purchased out-of-pocket this morning, unable to stomach the sight of his red double-happiness tin can any longer.\n\n\"Master, current water temperature is fifty-five degrees Celsius. Warmth maintained for two hours. Please remember to hydrate in a timely manner!\" The thermos abruptly chimed in a perky, saccharine electronic female voice.\n\nOld Zhou's weathered face twitched violently as he twisted the lid shut with lethal force, coughing dryly to mask his mortification before turning to Pei Yi'an at his flank: \"Little Pei, can we disable the voice on this damned contraption? I've collared hundreds of murderers in my lifetime, and today a pink cup nearly gave me a nervous breakdown.\"\n\nPei Yi'an ignored Old Zhou's self-deprecating banter entirely. Clad in an immaculately spotless long black trench coat and wearing fresh sky-blue sterile nitrile gloves, his clinical gaze vaulted across the cordoned marble floor, fixing directly onto the three-and-a-half-meter-tall colossal bronze sculpture erected at the dead center of the rotunda.\n\nThe piece was titled *The Flayed Prometheus*, a three-year magnum opus by Yan Keji, Binjiang's premier avant-garde sculptor who had trained in Europe, slated for its global unveiling as the centerpiece of this morning's grand opening.\n\nIt was a monumental bronze male torso exuding raw power and cruel aesthetics, the metal across the thorax deliberately stretched and torn into openwork ribbons resembling peeled muscular striations. Yet merely twenty minutes earlier, while museum conservators were dusting the fixtures, the intense heat of the theatrical spotlights had coaxed a dark, viscous droplet from deep within the bronze ribcage, releasing a suffocating stench of formalin and bone glue.\n\nWhen the conservators aimed a high-intensity inspection torch into the hollow cavity, the sight that met their eyes elicited an instantaneous chorus of bloodcurdling screams from everyone present—\n\nBeneath the labyrinthine, masterful striations of cast bronze lay an authentic, intact, and starkly white human skeleton!\n\n\"Where is Master Yan?\" Old Zhou shed his jovial mask in an instant, his gaze sweeping the perimeter like a predatory falcon.\n\n\"In the adjacent VIP lounge, suffering from arrhythmia and having just swallowed two nitro-glycerin pills.\" Su Tang hurried over carrying a forensic spectroscopy case, her face pale as she caught her breath. \"Yan Keji insists the piece was cast in his suburban studio, but the clay modeling and bronze core casting were outsourced to an industrial foundry. He claims he had zero idea human bones had been sealed inside!\"\n\n\"A clay mold cannot accommodate the thermal expansion coefficient of human bone in liquid bronze.\" Stepping onto the plinth in specialized shoe covers, Pei Yi'an's voice resonated with crystalline clarity. \"The melting point of bronze is 1,083 degrees Celsius. At that temperature, hydroxyapatite crystals within human osseous tissue disintegrate, while organic collagen carbonizes in milliseconds. This skeleton was meticulously inserted into the bronze shell piece by piece using forensic anatomical techniques through an access hatch concealed on the sculpture's back, long after casting and cooling were complete.\"\n\nPei Yi'an switched on his high-intensity inspection lamp, beaming light through the slits between the bronze ribs into the inner sanctum.\n\nWithin the depths of the bronze Prometheus's chest, twelve pairs of human ribs were arranged with flawless precision. Every sternocostal articulation was sutured with 0.2-millimeter solid-silver surgical wire, while the costal cartilage had been replaced with translucent medical-grade silicone fixative, crystal-clear, like an ivory stalactite forest suspended in the belly of an iron furnace.\n\n\"Deceased is male, chronologically between twenty-five and twenty-eight years of age.\" Drawing a pair of slender silver forceps, Pei Yi'an reached through the bronze aperture, delicately scraping a microscopic trace of residue from the surface of the manubrium. \"The bone is pristine with zero flesh, devoid of soft-tissue decomposition odors. This is no natural skeletonization; it was achieved via laboratory-grade dermestid beetle dermestophagy, augmented by low-temperature three-percent hydrogen peroxide bleaching.\"\n\n\"You mean... the killer is a professional dissector?\" Old Zhou's tone hardened.\n\n\"Not merely a dissector, but an obsessive fetishist harboring a pathological reverence for the human skeletal architecture.\" Pei Yi'an's forceps came to rest over the midpoint of the victim's left fourth true rib. \"Old Zhou, switch your torch to macro-polarized focus and observe here.\"\n\nLeaning in through the polarizing filter of the tactical torch, Old Zhou sucked in a harsh, jagged breath.\n\nAlong the pale exterior shaft of the fourth rib, micro-laser engraving had inscribed a miniature musical staff with microscopic precision!\n\nThe staff opened with a bass clef, followed immediately by four deliberate notes: **D - E - A - D**.\n\nAnd at the far right of the staff was etched a microscopic clockwork gear emblem, accompanied by an incised dedication:\n\n**\"Op. 02: Dedicated to the Second Violinist of the Bone Symphony.\"**\n\n\"DEAD... the deceased.\" Old Zhou murmured, his jaw clenching rock-hard. \"Movement Two is here... The Ferryman wasn't joking. Inside a bronze statue at the modern art museum, he left us an entire human skeleton converted into sheet music!\"\n\nJust then, rapid, weighty footsteps echoed from the rotunda's entrance.\n\nA broad-shouldered, stern-faced middle-aged officer strode in flanked by a cohort of plainclothes detectives. Wearing an impeccably tailored Senior Commissioner uniform, the insignia on his epaulets glinted cold and hard beneath the overhead lights—Lu Tianming, the newly appointed Executive Deputy Bureau Chief of Binjiang.\n\n\"Zhou Chenglin! Pei Yi'an!\" Lu Tianming's expression was as dark as a thunderhead, his commanding voice booming beneath the museum dome before he had even arrived: \"The Municipal Publicity Department and the Provincial Ministry have blown my phone lines off the hook! There are one hundred and twenty domestic and international journalists in this building! Forty-eight hours... Provincial headquarters gave us exactly forty-eight hours to identify the remains and close this case!\"\n\nOld Zhou arched an eyebrow, leisurely taking a sip of warm water from his pink thermos: \"Deputy Chief Lu, save the fireworks. Our Little Pei has already deduced the victim's osteological age and postmortem preservation methods at a single glance. With this forty-eight-hour window, I wager we have time to treat the culprit to two rounds of bureau pork-and-cabbage dumplings.\"\n\nGlaring daggers at Old Zhou, Lu Tianming drew a deep breath and turned his gaze toward Pei Yi'an, who remained transfixed by the bronze skeleton: \"Consultant Pei, who was the deceased in life? Do we have any identifying physical markers?\"\n\nRetracting his forceps, Pei Yi'an peeled off his gloves, his clear eyes calmly meeting Lu Tianming's heavy, scrutinizing gaze.\n\n\"The xiphoid process bears a distinct inward depression, and the cortex at the lateral third of both clavicles exhibits marked bilateral thickening accompanied by chronic stress-induced osteophytes.\" Slipping a fresh peppermint lozenge into his cheek, Pei Yi'an announced with absolute detachment:\n\n\"This was no ordinary citizen. The deceased spent years clamping a hardwood instrument firmly between his left clavicle and mandible, repeating bowing and finger-pressure biomechanics for over eight hours a day.\"\n\nTurning slightly, Pei Yi'an pointed toward the fourth rib bearing the musical staff within the hollow bronze chest:\n\n\"The deceased was a professional concert violinist. And his disappearance occurred no more than seven days ago.\""},{"id":8,"rawContent":"# 第八章：顯微鏡下的職業傷痕\n\n市公安局地下一層的病理檢驗中心，低溫冷氣將室溫精準鎖定在攝氏十六度。\n\n那尊高達三米半的青銅巨像《被剝皮的普羅米修斯》，已經被重型起重滑輪平穩地吊裝在特製的加固解剖台上。雕像後背那道隱蔽的梯形滑槽已經被完全開啟，在刺目耀眼的無影燈下，那副被純銀絲線精心拼裝的人體骸骨，終於被完整地剝離了金屬母體，安靜地陳列在一塊鋪滿吸水白布的長條鋼台上。\n\n「小裴，我說這兇手是不是學裁縫出身的？」老周戴著雙層加厚手套，手裡依舊捧著那隻扎眼的粉紅智慧型保溫杯，湊在鋼台旁嘖嘖稱奇，「你看這銀絲，從第一頸椎一路穿到尾骨，比我家老太太納的鞋底都板正。」\n\n「主人，檢測到環境濕度偏高，建議您注意關節保暖，按時飲用熱水哦！」保溫杯的液晶螢幕閃爍了一下，再度用甜美嬌憨的語音發出提醒。\n\n裴以安手中正拿著一把精密顯微手術鑷，聞言指尖微不可察地停頓了半秒。他面無表情地側過頭，鏡片後的目光冷得像兩把出鞘的剔骨尖刀。\n\n「周副隊長，如果您的電子飲水容器在未來五分鐘內再次發出這種頻率在二千四百赫茲至三千赫茲之間的劣質合成女聲，我會立刻使用骨科擺鋸將它的主機板與鋰電池實施永久性機械分離。」\n\n老周縮了縮脖子，趕緊伸出粗糙的食指按住保溫杯頂部的靜音鍵，嘿嘿乾笑：「消消氣，消消氣，這就讓它閉嘴。說正經的，死因查出來沒有？骨頭上連條骨折縫都看不見，這人總不能是被自己美死的吧？」\n\n「外力骨折是粗暴的底層犯罪者才會留下的痕跡。」裴以安轉過身，重新將注意力凝聚在鋼台上的白色頭顱與頸椎連接處，「蘇棠，打開超景深三維顯微鏡，偏振光調至百分之四十。」\n\n「好嘞！已連線大螢幕！」蘇棠熟練地敲擊著鍵盤，將顯微鏡的探頭緩緩降落在死者的枕骨大孔後緣。\n\n牆壁上的八十五寸超清液晶大螢幕上，骨骼表面被瞬間放大了兩百倍。\n\n只見在死者寰椎與枕骨髁的交界處——也就是延髓與高位頸脊髓的致命通道外側，赫然露出了一個直徑僅有零點六毫米的微小圓形穿刺孔！孔洞周圍的骨皮質極其平整，甚至連微小的骨裂紋都沒有向四周蔓延。\n\n「看見了嗎？」裴以安用鑷子尖端輕輕點了點屏幕上的微孔，「直徑零點六毫米，長度約八至十公分，極細且剛性極強的三棱醫用破壁穿刺針。兇手是在死者毫無防備的情況下，以精確的解剖角度從後頸正中刺入，精準切斷了迷走神經背核與呼吸循環中樞。」\n\n蘇棠倒吸了一口冷氣：「沒有呼救、沒有掙扎，呼吸和心跳在一秒鐘內瞬間停止……」\n\n「精確、冷酷、優雅，宛如在給時鐘拔掉發條。」裴以安放下鑷子，走到死者的肩帶骨與左側鎖骨旁，「現在，看他的職業烙印。」\n\n強光燈斜切打在死者的左側鎖骨與下頜骨下緣。\n\n「左側鎖骨中段骨面有長度三點二公分、寬度一點五公分的梭形骨質硬化帶，骨小梁密度比右側高出百分之三十五；左側下頜角下緣有一處直徑一點二公分的圓形骨質壓跡。」裴以安一邊測量數據，一邊以極快的語速說道，「這是長期使用腮托固定樂器造成的局部壓迫壞死與代償性骨肥厚。另外，死者左手第二至第五指末節指骨掌面，均有微小的橫向條狀壓痕——那是高強度金屬琴弦常年摩擦留下的痕跡。」\n\n「果然是小提琴手！」老周狠狠一拍大腿，「性別男，年齡二十五到二十八歲，身高一米七五左右，專業小提琴演奏員，失蹤時間在五到七天之內！小蘇，局裡的失蹤人口庫裡有沒有符合這幾個條件的？」\n\n蘇棠的十指在鍵盤上飛快跳躍，屏幕上的數據流如同瀑布般瘋狂刷新。\n\n不過五秒鐘，一條標註著鮮紅警報的失蹤協查通報猛然彈了出來！\n\n「找到了！」蘇棠興奮地大喊，「葉馳！二十七歲，濱江愛樂樂團第二小提琴副首席！五天前的深夜，他在市文化中心結束私人排練後獨自駕車回家，隨後車輛在沿江高架橋下被遺棄，手機信號徹底中斷！」\n\n老周湊到屏幕前，看著檔案照片上那個留著微卷長髮、抱著小提琴意氣風發的英俊年輕人，眉頭深深擰了起來：「濱江愛樂樂團……又是濱江愛樂樂團！大提琴首席陸思遠、二提琴副首席葉馳……這擺渡人是打算把整個樂團的主力全給拆成零件？！」\n\n「這不是巧合。」裴以安的聲音依舊清冷，他重新走回那根刻著微雕樂譜的第四真肋旁，「蘇棠，共聚焦激光掃描第四肋骨骨面。」\n\n藍色的激光束在骨骼表面細密地掃過，大屏幕上的微雕五線譜再次被放大。\n\n這一次，在那個刻著「D - E - A - D」四個音符的五線譜下方，一行以納米級激光微雕技術刻出的德文樂曲名稱赫然浮現：\n\n**《D小調夏康舞曲》（Chaconne in D Minor）——約翰·塞巴斯蒂安·巴赫。**\n\n而在樂曲名稱的最末端，赫然刻著一個精確到分秒的演出時間：\n\n**「演出時間：今晚八點整。舞台：濱江大劇院一號音樂廳。」**\n\n「今晚八點？！」老周猛地抬頭看了一眼牆上的掛鐘，指針已經指向了下午一點四十分，「距離今晚八點只剩不到六個半小時了！」\n\n「這首夏康舞曲，是小提琴獨奏作品中公認難度最高、也是最著名的輓歌。」裴以安摘下口罩，修長的指尖輕輕撫平白大褂的下擺，「相傳巴赫是在旅途中得知妻子猝逝後寫下了這首曲子。這是一首從死亡深淵中尋求復活的終極樂章。」\n\n就在這時，解剖室的防爆雙開門突然被粗暴地一把推開！\n\n值班刑警氣喘吁吁地衝了進來，甚至顧不上穿防護鞋套，手裡抓著一份剛剛接收的加急傳真，臉色煞白：\n\n「周隊！裴顧問！濱江大劇院出事了！」\n\n老周心頭猛地一沉：「劇院怎麼了？說！」\n\n「十分鐘前，濱江愛樂樂團的首席第一小提琴家溫雪晴，在她的個人化妝間裡收到了一個匿名同城快遞包裹！」值班警員滿頭大汗地匯報，「拆開包裹後……裡面裝著一把完全由人體指骨串聯而成的小提琴琴弓！隨包裹附帶的字條上寫著——如果今晚八點的大劇院夏康舞曲沒有如期奏響，劇院的一千兩百個觀眾席座椅下方，將會同時綻放鮮紅的火花！」","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 8: Occupational Scars Under the Lens\n\nIn the Subterranean Pathology Center on Basement Level 1 of the Municipal Police Bureau, sub-zero air conditioning locked the ambient room temperature at a precise sixteen degrees Celsius.\n\nThe three-and-a-half-meter colossal bronze statue, *The Flayed Prometheus*, had been hoisted by heavy-duty rigging pulleys and stabilized onto a custom reinforced autopsy platform. The concealed trapezoidal access hatch along the sculpture's back was fully unlatched; under the glaring brilliance of the shadowless surgical lamps, the human skeleton—painstakingly assembled with solid-silver wire—had finally been detached from its metallic matrix, laid out quietly upon a long stainless-steel dissecting table draped in absorbent white linen.\n\n\"Little Pei, do you think this killer started out as a tailor?\" Wearing double-thick surgical gloves while still clutching his eye-searing pink smart thermos, Old Zhou leaned over the steel table, clicking his tongue in marvel. \"Look at this silver wire—threaded all the way from the first cervical vertebra down to the coccyx, straighter than the hemp soles my old lady stitches.\"\n\n\"Master, ambient humidity is elevated. We recommend keeping your joints warm and hydrating on schedule!\" The thermos's digital LCD screen blinked, chiming once more in a saccharine, perky electronic female voice.\n\nPei Yi'an was holding a pair of precision micro-dissecting forceps; his fingers paused for an imperceptible fraction of a second. Turning his head with complete impassivity, the gaze behind his spectacles was cold enough to match two unsheathed boning knives.\n\n\"Deputy Captain Zhou, if your electronic beverage container produces that substandard synthesized female timbre between 2,400 and 3,000 Hertz once more within the next five minutes, I will immediately employ an orthopedic oscillating bone saw to mechanically separate its motherboard from its lithium-ion battery permanently.\"\n\nDucking his neck, Old Zhou hastily jammed his calloused index finger over the mute sensor on the cap, chuckling dryly in sheepish surrender: \"Easy now, easy, she's muzzled for good. Down to business: have you pinned the cause of death? Not a single hairline fracture on any of these bones—the guy couldn't have died of pure vanity, could he?\"\n\n\"External bone fractures are crude signatures left only by pedestrian, bottom-tier criminals.\" Turning away, Pei Yi'an focused his scrutiny back onto the junction connecting the ivory-white cranium and cervical spine. \"Su Tang, initialize the 3D digital depth-of-field microscope. Set polarized light to forty percent.\"\n\n\"Copy that! Main display connected!\" Su Tang typed swiftly across her keyboard, gradually descending the microscope's optical sensor toward the posterior margin of the victim's foramen magnum.\n\nAcross the wall-mounted eighty-five-inch ultra-high-definition monitor, the cortical bone surface magnified instantaneously by two hundred times.\n\nThere, at the articulation between the atlas and occipital condyles—the fatal threshold guarding the medulla oblongata and high cervical spinal cord—a microscopic circular puncture hole measuring a mere 0.6 millimeters in diameter lay starkly exposed! The surrounding cortical bone was surgically smooth, without even microscopic fracture lines radiating outward.\n\n\"Do you see it?\" Pei Yi'an lightly tapped the monitor screen with the tip of his forceps. \"0.6 millimeters in diameter, approximately eight to ten centimeters in length—an ultra-fine, ultra-rigid triangular medical trocar needle. The killer thrust it squarely through the posterior midline of the neck at an infallible anatomical angle while the victim was completely off-guard, cleanly severing the dorsal motor nucleus of the vagus nerve and the cardiorespiratory center.\"\n\nSu Tang sucked in an icy breath: \"No cries, no struggle... respiration and cardiac rhythm terminated in less than a second...\"\n\n\"Precise, merciless, and elegant, exactly like pulling the mainspring from a pocket watch.\" Setting his forceps aside, Pei Yi'an stepped toward the victim's shoulder girdle and left clavicle. \"Now, observe his occupational imprint.\"\n\nThe high-intensity spotlight cut obliquely across the victim's left clavicle and inferior mandibular margin.\n\n\"Along the midshaft of the left clavicle lies a spindle-shaped zone of osteosclerosis 3.2 centimeters long by 1.5 centimeters wide, with trabecular density thirty-five percent higher than the right; beneath the left mandibular angle sits a circular bone depression 1.2 centimeters across.\" Pei Yi'an measured the telemetry, rattling off data at breakneck speed: \"This is localized pressure necrosis and compensatory bone hypertrophy induced by years of anchoring an instrument against a chin rest. Furthermore, the palmar aspects of the distal phalanges of the left second through fifth digits display delicate transverse linear furrows—permanent impressions worn by high-tension metallic musical strings.\"\n\n\"A violinist after all!\" Old Zhou slapped his thigh hard. \"Male, aged twenty-five to twenty-eight, approximately 175 centimeters tall, professional violinist, missing within the last five to seven days! Little Su, run those parameters through the bureau's missing persons database!\"\n\nSu Tang's fingers danced across the keyboard like lightning, cascading streams of data flooding across the screen.\n\nIn less than five seconds, a missing persons bulletin tagged with a crimson flashing alert popped onto the terminal!\n\n\"Found him!\" Su Tang shouted in triumph. \"Ye Chi! Twenty-seven years old, Associate Concertmaster of the Second Violins for the Binjiang Philharmonic! Five nights ago, after finishing a private rehearsal at the Municipal Cultural Center, he drove home alone. His vehicle was subsequently found abandoned beneath the riverside elevated expressway, his phone signal terminating completely!\"\n\nOld Zhou leaned in close to the screen, studying the dossier photo of the handsome youth with loose wavy hair holding his violin with fiery ambition, his brow knitting tightly: \"The Binjiang Philharmonic... the Binjiang Philharmonic again! Cello principal Lu Siyuan, second violin associate concertmaster Ye Chi... is this Ferryman intending to dismantle the entire orchestra down to spare parts?!\"\n\n\"This is no coincidence.\" Pei Yi'an's voice remained crystalline as he stepped back toward the fourth true rib bearing the micro-engraving. \"Su Tang, confocal laser scan across the cortical surface of the fourth rib.\"\n\nThe azure laser beam swept meticulously across the bone, and the engraved staff on the main monitor magnified once more.\n\nThis time, directly beneath the musical staff bearing the four notes \"D - E - A - D\", an inscription etched in nanometer-scale laser calligraphy surfaced in German:\n\n**Chaconne in D Minor — Johann Sebastian Bach.**\n\nAnd inscribed at the very terminus of the composition's title was a performance timestamp calibrated down to the exact minute:\n\n**\"Curtain: Tonight at 8:00 p.m. sharp. Stage: Concert Hall One, Binjiang Grand Theatre.\"**\n\n\"Eight o'clock tonight?!\" Old Zhou whipped his head toward the wall clock; the hands already pointed to 1:40 in the afternoon. \"We have less than six and a half hours until eight o'clock!\"\n\n\"This Chaconne is universally recognized as the most demanding solo violin composition ever penned, and history's most celebrated elegy.\" Removing his surgical mask, Pei Yi'an smoothed the hem of his white lab coat with his slender fingertips. \"Legend holds that Bach composed this piece upon returning from travel to discover his wife had died suddenly. It is a monumental movement seeking resurrection from the abyss of mortality.\"\n\nRight at that second, the double-leaf explosion-proof doors of the pathology suite were violently kicked open!\n\nA duty detective dashed inside, breathless and drenched in sweat, completely neglecting his protective shoe covers as he waved an urgent fax dispatch, his face bleached white:\n\n\"Captain Zhou! Consultant Pei! An emergency at the Binjiang Grand Theatre!\"\n\nOld Zhou's gut lurched violently: \"What happened at the theatre?! Speak!\"\n\n\"Ten minutes ago, Wen Xueqing, the principal first violinist of the Binjiang Philharmonic, received an anonymous same-city courier delivery in her private dressing room!\" The detective reported frantically. \"Upon opening the package... inside was a violin bow strung entirely out of articulated human finger phalanges! The note enclosed warned—if the Bach Chaconne does not sound at the Grand Theatre at eight o'clock tonight as scheduled, scarlet blossoms of fire will detonate simultaneously beneath all 1,200 auditorium seats!\""},{"id":9,"rawContent":"# 第九章：暴雨前的限時四十八小時\n\n下午三點十五分，傾盆暴雨將濱江大劇院那座宛如銀色貝殼般的巨型穹頂澆得泛起漫天白霧。\n\n三十輛閃爍著紅藍警燈的警車與防爆排爆裝甲車將大劇院四個主要出入口封鎖得水洩不通。身穿重型防爆服的排爆特警手持非線性節點探測儀穿梭在通道中，空氣中瀰漫著濃烈的臭氧味與暴雨的潮氣。\n\n劇院後台二樓的首席化妝間內，氣氛凝固得宛如一塊隨時會碎裂的寒冰。\n\n「局長下了死命令，在沒有完全排除爆燃風險前，絕不能引發大規模群體恐慌。」常務副局長陸天明站在門口，雙手叉腰，鐵青著臉看向化妝鏡前那個瑟瑟發抖的年輕女子，「溫雪晴女士，你確定這個包裹沒有經過劇院收發室，是直接出現在你化妝台上的？」\n\n被問話的女子正是濱江愛樂樂團第一小提琴首席溫雪晴。她穿著一身華貴的黑色晚禮服，精緻的妝容已被淚水徹底沖花，雙手死死攥著一塊濕透的手帕，連說話的力氣都幾乎被抽空。\n\n在她面前鋪著天鵝絨軟布的化妝台上，赫然擺放著那柄令人毛骨悚然的「提琴琴弓」。\n\n琴弓的弓桿並非名貴的巴西蘇木，而是由十四根被打磨得光滑慘白的人體手指近節與中節指骨，以直徑零點一毫米的純銀外科導線嚴絲合縫地串聯而成。骨節之間用透明環氧樹脂加固，弓尾庫則是一枚雕刻成銜尾蛇圖騰的微型黃銅卡榫，白色的特級蒙古馬尾毛在燈光下泛著冰冷死寂的光暈。\n\n「周成林，裴以安，你們倆過來看。」陸天明側身讓開一條道，眉頭擰成了死結，「排爆隊用X光透視過了，琴弓內部沒有炸藥引信，但這玩意兒……到底是用誰的骨頭做的？」\n\n老周一手插在風衣口袋裡，另一手拎著那隻被強制靜音的粉紅保溫杯，慢悠悠地晃進了化妝間。他瞥了一眼化妝台上的骨弓，嘴裡嚼著半截茶葉，眼神卻冷靜如冰。\n\n裴以安則戴著全新的無菌橡膠手套，緩步走上前去。他沒有立刻觸摸琴弓，而是從胸前口袋掏出一柄微型醫用游標卡尺，俯下身對著第一枚指骨進行測量。\n\n「第一指骨長度四點一公分，骨幹中段橫徑一點二公分，骨皮質密度偏高。」裴以安的聲音沒有半分波瀾，彷彿眼前只是一堆普通的實驗室標本，「近端關節面邊緣有微小的唇狀骨質增生，這是長期重複小提琴左手高把位按弦造成的特殊勞損。骨骼表面的過氧化氫殘留氣味與現代藝術館青銅雕像內的骸骨完全一致。」\n\n「也就是說……」老周吐掉嘴裡的茶葉渣，臉色陰沉了下來。\n\n「這正是葉馳被切下的左手手指。」裴以安直起身，摘下手套扔進隨身證物袋，「兇手在二號乾塢殺死葉馳後，不僅用皮蠹甲蟲啃噬了他的軀幹骨骼，還特意取下了他生前最引以為傲的左手手指，做成了這把小提琴弓，送給了坐在這裡的第一首席。」\n\n溫雪晴聽到「葉馳」兩個字，整個人如遭雷擊，發出一聲淒厲的抽泣，差點從椅子上栽倒下去。\n\n「溫首席，你似乎並不驚訝葉馳已經遇害？」裴以安轉過身，鏡片後的雙眸銳利得彷彿能穿透皮肉，直視對方的神經末梢，「當陸副局長剛才詢問包裹來源時，你的瞳孔放大了百分之二十，但雙眼下意識瞥向了化妝室左側的暗門。那裡原本擺放著葉馳的私人琴盒，對嗎？」\n\n「我……我不知道你在說什麼！」溫雪晴崩潰地捂住耳朵大喊，「我和葉馳只是樂團同事！他失蹤跟我沒有任何關係！」\n\n「同事？」老周走上前一步，雙手撐在化妝台上，嘴角扯出一抹老刑警特有的譏誚笑意，「溫小姐，市局金融犯罪調查科半小時前剛剛查了你的私人帳戶。上個月二十號，瀚海集團名下的『當代青年藝術基金會』，以匿名贊助的名義給你的海外信託匯了兩百萬美元。而同一天，你手中那把價值一千五百萬的十七世紀阿瑪蒂古董小提琴，正是由陸崇山親自擔任的擔保人。」\n\n化妝間內瞬間陷入一片死寂，只有窗外暴雨狂暴的沖刷聲在轟鳴。\n\n溫雪晴的臉色由白轉灰，原本死守的心理防線在巨額資金流水的證據面前徹底崩塌。\n\n「葉馳……葉馳發現了那筆錢的來源……」溫雪晴失魂落魄地垂下頭，眼淚滴落在昂貴的晚禮服上，「那個藝術基金會根本不是在扶持青年藝術家，那是三十年前陸崇山侵吞市立醫院新藥專利後設立的海外洗錢蓄水池！葉馳拿到了瀚海當年的實驗原始底稿，他想揭發……他說這把琴上的每一根弦，都浸滿了三十年前試驗死難者的血！」\n\n「所以你出賣了他？」陸天明咬牙怒喝。\n\n「我沒有！我只是想勸他收手！」溫雪晴尖叫著反駁，聲音尖銳得變了調，「我告訴他陸家的勢力有多大，我告訴他我們根本鬥不過瀚海！但他不聽……五天前排練結束後，他上了陸家保鑣的車，然後就再也沒有回來……」\n\n就在這時，排爆大隊隊長滿頭大汗地從樓下音樂廳一路狂奔上來，重重推開了化妝間的門：\n\n「陸局！周隊！音樂廳底下的情況查清楚了！」\n\n陸天明猛地轉身：「找到了定時炸彈？！」\n\n「比定時炸彈棘手十倍！」排爆隊長抹了一把臉上的冷汗，胸膛劇烈起伏，「兇手把一千二百個觀眾席座椅下方的中央通風管全部改裝了！裡面灌滿了高壓低溫氣化的特種高爆化學溶劑，並連接著十二組精密音頻感應繼電器！」\n\n「音頻感應？」裴以安眸光一閃。\n\n「對！感應器的接收頻率被死死鎖定在巴赫《D小調夏康舞曲》的旋律上！」排爆隊長聲音發顫，「控制系統連接著大劇院的主控調音台。今晚八點整，只要音樂廳內的夏康舞曲沒有準時奏響，或者演奏過程中音準偏差超過半個音階、中途停頓超過三秒鐘……整個地下通風管道的化學溶劑就會瞬間被高壓電弧點燃，引發連環粉塵殉爆！」\n\n老周的瞳孔狠狠收縮，手中的保溫杯在掌心劇烈顫抖了一下：「那瘋子要一千兩百名觀眾當這首輓歌的人質……而且，他逼著溫雪晴用死者的指骨，在舞台上拉響這首死亡之曲！」\n\n裴以安看了一眼化妝台上那柄森白的骨弓，又看了一眼已經完全癱軟在地的溫雪晴。\n\n「溫雪晴的雙手前臂肌腱已經出現功能性震顫，她現在連空弦都拉不直。」裴以安的聲音平靜得令人膽寒，他轉過頭，看向面如重鉛的陸天明與老周：\n\n「老周，叫防爆專家立刻封閉中央通風管道的排氣閥門，利用乾冰給溶劑降溫延緩氣化速度。」\n\n裴以安邁開長腿走向門口，解開了風衣最上方的一顆紐扣：\n\n「現在是下午三點半。在今晚八點大幕拉開之前，我們必須在濱江市找到第二位能拉響夏康舞曲的活人——或者，找到那個在暗處握著遙控器的擺渡人。」","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 9: 48 Hours Before the Downpour\n\nAt 3:15 in the afternoon, the torrential downpour drenched the Binjiang Grand Theatre's colossal silver-shell dome until steam drifted across the sky like mist.\n\nThirty police cruisers and heavy armored bomb disposal units with flashing crimson and azure lights cordoned off the theatre's four main perimeter checkpoints until not a drop of water could leak through. Explosive Ordnance Disposal officers in full blast-protection suits navigated the corridors clutching non-linear junction detectors, the atmosphere saturated with the acrid reek of ozone and storm dampness.\n\nInside the backstage second-floor dressing room of the concertmaster, the tension was frozen solid like brittle ice on the verge of fracturing.\n\n\"The Bureau Chief has issued an absolute directive: until explosive deflagration hazards are completely eliminated, under no circumstances will mass panic be tolerated.\" Executive Deputy Chief Lu Tianming stood braced in the doorway, hands on his hips, his face dark as iron as he stared at the trembling young woman seated before the vanity mirror. \"Ms. Wen Xueqing, are you certain this parcel bypassed the backstage mailroom and manifested directly upon your vanity?\"\n\nThe woman interrogated was Wen Xueqing, First Violin Concertmaster of the Binjiang Philharmonic Orchestra. Dressed in an opulent black evening gown, her exquisite stage makeup was completely washed away by tears, her hands clutching a sodden handkerchief as if even the physical strength to speak had been bled dry.\n\nDirectly before her on the velvet-draped vanity table lay that hair-raising, grotesque \"violin bow.\"\n\nThe stick was forged from no rare Brazilian pernambuco, but assembled from fourteen polished, deathly-pale human proximal and middle phalanges, bound flush together by 0.1-millimeter solid-silver surgical wire. The knuckles were reinforced with clear epoxy resin, the frog anchored by a miniature brass slide sculpted into an ouroboros, and the white, premium Mongolian horsehair gleamed with an icy, tomb-like luster beneath the dressing room lights.\n\n\"Zhou Chenglin, Pei Yi'an, get in here and inspect this.\" Lu Tianming stepped aside, his brow tied into a knotted scowl. \"Bomb squad ran it through portable X-ray; there are no explosive detonators inside the bow, but this contraption... whose bones was it cobbled together from?\"\n\nWith one hand buried in his trench coat pocket and the other dangling his forcefully muted pink thermos, Old Zhou ambled casually into the dressing room. He cast a sidelong glance at the bone bow on the vanity, chewing half a tea leaf, his eyes as cold and calculating as ice.\n\nGloved in a fresh pair of sterile rubber gloves, Pei Yi'an stepped slowly forward. Rather than handling the bow immediately, he retrieved a miniature medical vernier caliper from his breast pocket and stooped down to measure the first phalanx.\n\n\"First phalanx length 4.1 centimeters, midshaft transverse diameter 1.2 centimeters, bone cortex density conspicuously elevated.\" Pei Yi'an's voice lacked even a tremor of emotion, as if he were cataloging mundane laboratory specimens. \"The proximal articular margin exhibits microscopic lip-shaped osteophytes—pathognomonic wear from repetitive high-position left-hand string-stopping on a violin. The residual hydrogen peroxide scent along the osseous surface matches the skeleton inside the modern art museum's bronze statue with absolute fidelity.\"\n\n\"Which means...\" Spitting out the dregs of the tea leaf, Old Zhou's expression darkened completely.\n\n\"These are the severed fingers of Ye Chi's left hand.\" Pei Yi'an straightened, stripping off his gloves and discarding them into a sterile evidence pouch. \"After executing Ye Chi in Dry Dock Number Two, the killer not only subjected his axial skeleton to dermestid beetle defleshing, but deliberately amputated the left digits he took the greatest pride in, fashioned them into this violin bow, and presented it to the concertmaster seated right here.\"\n\nHearing the name \"Ye Chi,\" Wen Xueqing recoiled as if struck by lightning, letting out a jagged, agonized sob that nearly caused her to collapse from her chair.\n\n\"Concertmaster Wen, you appear remarkably unsurprised that Ye Chi has been murdered?\" Pei Yi'an turned, his gaze behind his lenses cutting through flesh and bone to scrutinize her autonomic responses. \"When Deputy Chief Lu questioned the package's provenance moments ago, your pupils dilated by twenty percent, yet your eyes subconsciously darted toward the concealed door on the left of this vanity. That was where Ye Chi's personal instrument case originally rested, correct?\"\n\n\"I... I have no idea what you're talking about!\" Wen Xueqing clamped her hands over her ears, shrieking in hysteria, \"Ye Chi and I were merely orchestra colleagues! His disappearance has absolutely nothing to do with me!\"\n\n\"Colleagues?\" Striding forward, Old Zhou braced both hands on the vanity table, his mouth curling into the dry, mocking grin of a seasoned detective. \"Ms. Wen, the bureau's Financial Crimes Division audited your offshore accounts thirty minutes ago. On the twentieth of last month, the 'Contemporary Youth Arts Foundation' under Hanhai Group wired two million US dollars to your offshore trust as an anonymous sponsorship. And that seventeenth-century Amati antique violin in your hands valued at fifteen million—its guarantor was none other than Lu Chongshan himself.\"\n\nThe dressing room plunged into tomb-like silence, save for the furious roar of the storm scouring the glass outside.\n\nWen Xueqing's face drained from paper-white to ash-grey, her stubborn psychological defense completely detonated before the paper trail of colossal wealth.\n\n\"Ye Chi... Ye Chi discovered where that money originated...\" Lowering her head in shattered despair, her tears spattered against her costly silk gown. \"That foundation never nurtured young artists; it was an offshore laundering reservoir established thirty years ago when Lu Chongshan usurped the Municipal Hospital's pharmaceutical patents! Ye Chi uncovered Hanhai's original trial records; he intended to blow the whistle... he swore every string on my violin was saturated with the blood of the 1994 victims!\"\n\n\"So you betrayed him?\" Lu Tianming ground his teeth in rage.\n\n\"I didn't! I merely begged him to let it go!\" Wen Xueqing screamed in defense, her pitch warping in terror. \"I warned him how terrifying the Lu family's reach was, I told him we could never fight Hanhai! But he wouldn't listen... five nights ago after rehearsal, he climbed into a vehicle driven by Lu's bodyguards, and he never came back...\"\n\nAt that very instant, the Bomb Squad Commander burst up the stairwell from the concert hall below, drenched in sweat, throwing the dressing room doors wide:\n\n\"Chief Lu! Captain Zhou! The situation beneath the auditorium has been confirmed!\"\n\nLu Tianming whipped around: \"Did you locate a timed explosive?!\"\n\n\"Ten times worse than a timed explosive!\" The commander wiped freezing sweat from his brow, his chest heaving violently. \"The perpetrator modified the central plenum ventilation ducting beneath all 1,200 audience seats! The entire network is pressurized with cryogenic vaporized military-grade liquid explosive, wired to twelve banks of precision acoustic-resonance relays!\"\n\n\"Acoustic relays?\" Pei Yi'an's eyes narrowed.\n\n\"Yes! The receivers are frequency-locked exclusively to the melody of Bach's *Chaconne in D Minor*!\" The commander's voice trembled. \"The telemetry links directly into the theatre's master acoustic mixing console. Tonight at eight o'clock sharp, if the Bach Chaconne does not begin on the second, or if the pitch drifts by more than half a semitone, or if the performance halts for more than three seconds... the entire subterranean plenum will be detonated by high-voltage electrical arcs, triggering a catastrophic continuous fuel-air explosion!\"\n\nOld Zhou's pupils constricted violently, his grip on the pink thermos trembling in his palm: \"That lunatic is taking 1,200 spectators as hostages for an elegy... and forcing Wen Xueqing to play this funeral hymn upon the stage using the dead man's finger bones!\"\n\nPei Yi'an glanced at the pale bone bow upon the vanity, and then at Wen Xueqing, who had collapsed into a catatonic heap on the carpet.\n\n\"Wen Xueqing's forearm flexor tendons are already exhibiting functional tremors; currently, she cannot even sustain an open-string stroke.\" Pei Yi'an's tone was terrifying in its lucidity. Turning his head, he met the leaden gazes of Lu Tianming and Old Zhou:\n\n\"Old Zhou, instruct EOD to seal the intake dampers of the central plenum immediately, and pump dry ice into the ducts to suppress ambient temperature and retard vaporization.\"\n\nStepping forward on long legs toward the corridor, Pei Yi'an unbuttoned the top collar of his trench coat:\n\n\"It is currently 3:30 p.m. Before the curtain rises at eight o'clock tonight, we must locate a second living soul in Binjiang capable of performing the Bach Chaconne—or unmask the Ferryman holding the detonator in the dark.\""},{"id":10,"rawContent":"# 第十章：誰在指揮骨骼交響曲\n\n下午四點四十分，距離八點整的死亡大幕拉開，只剩下最後三個小時又二十分鐘。\n\n大劇院頂層那間能夠俯瞰整條混濁長江的奢華總監辦公室內，厚重的深紅色絲絨窗簾被狂風吹得獵獵作響。空氣中瀰漫著古董雪茄、陳年威士忌，以及一種隱蔽在紫檀木家具深處的淡淡機油香氣。\n\n坐在雕花皮椅上的男人年近六旬，身形清瘦挺拔，一頭梳理得一絲不苟的銀白色長髮披在肩頭，身上穿著一件純手工縫製的燕尾服常服。他就是享譽國際的指揮巨擘、濱江愛樂樂團終身藝術總監兼首席指揮家——賀凌峰。\n\n「兩位警官，你們是說……葉馳死了，而今晚大劇院地下的通風管道裡，裝滿了能在三秒鐘內把我們所有人送上西天的化學炸藥？」賀凌峰優雅地轉動著無名指上的黃金圖章戒指，眼神平靜得宛如一潭死水，甚至連眉毛都沒有動一下。\n\n「賀總監，看來您的心理素質比樓下那位哭到脫水的第一首席要強大得多。」老周單手插兜走上前，將那隻被強制靜音的粉紅保溫杯重重頓在昂貴的紫檀木辦公桌上，「或者說，您早就知道今晚的觀眾席底下，埋著這首死人譜寫的《夏康舞曲》？」\n\n賀凌峰端起桌上的水晶酒杯，輕抿了一口琥珀色的烈酒：「老刑警，我這一生指揮過三千七百場交響樂。在卡內基音樂廳、在維也納金色大廳，我見過無數次弦斷、琴毀、樂手當場心肌梗塞。舞台就是一個被精確計算的修羅場，任何慌亂都只會讓音符走調。」\n\n「走調？」站在一旁的裴以安忽然冷笑了一聲。\n\n他並未落座，而是像一尊冰冷的巡檢儀器般在書架前踱步。他的目光掠過牆上那些與各國元首、音樂大師的合影，最終精準地停留在賀凌峰右耳後方那一截極其微小的純銀肉色耳勾上。\n\n「賀總監，您的右側聽神經已經完全壞死，依靠的是瑞士製造的高精度微型骨導助聽器。」裴以安雙手插在風衣口袋裡，轉過身，眼神銳利如手術刀，「這款助聽器的核心傳動結構採用的是雙軸微型游絲，它的專利來源，正是一九三四年莫里斯·斯坦為舊租界名流特別訂製的『黃銅微型共振聽診儀』。」\n\n賀凌峰握著酒杯的右手指關節，在這一瞬間極其短暫地僵硬了一下。\n\n「你對機械構造很懂，年輕的法醫。」賀凌峰抬起眼皮，目光深沉如夜。\n\n「我對機械不感興趣，我只對人體病理感興趣。」裴以安邁開步子走回桌前，雙手撐在桌面上，身體微微前傾，強大的壓迫感瞬間籠罩了整張辦公桌，「三十年前，市立醫院耳鼻喉科最年輕的副主任醫師，因為拒絕在陸崇山那份違規神經阻斷劑試驗報告上偽造『聽力修復數據』，在林清源博士遇害的當天深夜被秘密除名，隨後銷聲匿跡。」\n\n裴以安盯著賀凌峰那雙混濁卻深邃的眼眸，一字一頓地揭開謎底：\n\n「那個被抹去檔案的年輕醫生，本名不叫賀凌峰，而是叫林清淮——林清源博士同父異母的親弟弟，死者林懷遠的親叔叔！」\n\n「什麼？！」老周渾身一震，右手下意識按住了腰間的佩槍，「賀總監……你是林清源的親弟弟？！那這一切……這一切的連環殺人案，是你布下的局？！」\n\n「老周，冷靜一點。」裴以安甚至沒有回頭，聲音平靜如冰，「他不是擺渡人。如果他是今晚的指揮家，他那隻裝在右耳裡的骨導助聽器，就不會在一分鐘內產生三次高達八十分貝的異常高頻嘯叫。」\n\n裴以安伸出戴著手套的右手，閃電般探向賀凌峰的右耳，食指精準地按住耳勾後方一枚米粒大小的微型凸起！\n\n「滋——」\n\n一陣刺耳的音頻干擾雜音驟然從助聽器微型揚聲器裡噴出，隨之而來的，是一道冰冷、優雅且經過多重變頻濾波處理的陌生聲音：\n\n『林清淮醫師，或者說，偉大的賀總監。你的時間不多了。距離今晚八點鐘還有最後一百九十分鐘。如果你不能站在指揮台上引導溫雪晴奏響那把指骨琴弓，你遠在日內瓦音樂學院就讀的女兒，將會在同一秒鐘，收到一份用純銀絲線縫合的心臟標本。』\n\n通訊在雜音中瞬間切斷。\n\n老周倒吸了一口涼氣，額頭上的青筋暴突起來：「媽的！那王八蛋用賀總監女兒的命，在逼他上台當傀儡！」\n\n「林清源是我的兄長，他至死都在守護醫者的良知。」賀凌峰閉上雙眼，兩行渾濁的淚水終於順著溝壑縱橫的臉頰滑落，整個人彷彿在這一瞬間蒼老了二十歲，「三十年前我逃去了歐洲，改名換姓學了指揮，我以為用音樂的聖潔可以洗刷掉陸家帶給我們家族的屈辱與血淚。但惡魔從未放過我們……他找到了我，他逼我成為這場殺戮交響曲的活體節拍器！」\n\n「溫雪晴的前臂肌腱已經痙攣，她根本無法拉響夏康舞曲。」老周急得原地轉圈，「排爆隊說了，中途只要停頓超過三秒，一千二百個座位下的化學毒氣就會瞬間殉爆！這場音樂會如果取消是死，如期開演也是死！」\n\n「她不需要取消，她也不需要拉響整首曲子。」\n\n裴以安轉過身，冷靜地拉開了隨身勘驗箱的拉鏈。\n\n他從箱中取出一支裝滿透明藥液的精密微量注射器，以及一包長達十公分的醫用毫針。\n\n「溫雪晴的症狀是典型的創傷後神經源性肌緊張，並非器質性神經損傷。」裴以安的眼中跳動著冰冷而純粹的理智之火，「利用高純度甲鈷胺配合局麻微量阻滯，我可以在三十秒內解除她橈神經與正中神經的病理性震顫，恢復她至少兩個小時的手指機械記憶。」\n\n「那之後呢？」老周瞪大了眼睛，「就算她能拉響前面幾節，等曲子拉完了，炸藥難道會自動失效？！」\n\n「夏康舞曲全曲長達十三至十五分鐘，共由六十四段精妙絕倫的變奏組成。」裴以安將針頭對準燈光，緩緩推出一滴晶瑩的藥液，「而在整座劇院的排氣總閥門處，排爆隊需要十五分鐘才能將低溫乾冰完全灌滿管道、阻斷電弧引信。」\n\n裴以安轉過頭，看向面色慘白的賀凌峰與神情凝重的老周：\n\n「今晚的舞台上不需要恐慌。溫雪晴負責拉琴，賀總監負責揮棒，而我和老周……」\n\n裴以安推了推眼鏡，薄唇勾起一抹極度危險的鋒芒：\n\n「我們會在第十三分鐘最後一個樂章落下之前，順著音頻發信器的反向鏈路，把那個坐在觀眾席暗處手握引爆器的擺渡人，當場揪出來！」","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 10: Who Conducts the Bone Symphony?\n\nAt 4:40 in the afternoon, only three hours and twenty minutes remained before the curtain rose upon the mortal performance at eight o'clock sharp.\n\nInside the opulent Director's Suite on the top floor of the Grand Theatre, offering a panoramic vantage over the turbid expanse of the Binjiang, heavy crimson velvet drapes whipped wildly in the gale. The air was saturated with antique cigars, aged single-malt whisky, and a faint, secretive tang of clockwork lubricant tucked deep within the rosewood appointments.\n\nThe man seated in the carved leather armchair was approaching sixty, tall and lean, an immaculate mane of silver-white hair cascading over his shoulders, dressed in a bespoke handmade tailcoat suit. He was the internationally revered maestro, Lifetime Artistic Director, and Chief Conductor of the Binjiang Philharmonic Orchestra—He Lingfeng.\n\n\"Gentlemen, you are saying... Ye Chi is dead, and the subterranean ventilation plenum of this theatre is packed with enough liquid chemical explosive to send every soul here to heaven in three seconds flat?\" He Lingfeng turned the gold signet ring on his ring finger with languid elegance, his eyes as impassive as stagnant water, not even a brow twitching.\n\n\"Director He, it appears your psychological fortitude is remarkably superior to that of your dehydrated first concertmaster downstairs.\" Striding forward with one hand in his trench coat pocket, Old Zhou slammed his forcefully muted pink thermos onto the costly rosewood desktop with a heavy thud. \"Or perhaps you knew all along that beneath tonight's auditorium seats lay this *Chaconne* orchestrated by the dead?\"\n\nHe Lingfeng lifted a crystal tumbler, sipping the amber spirit leisurely: \"Officer, I have conducted 3,700 symphonies in my career. In Carnegie Hall, in the Musikverein of Vienna, I have witnessed snapped strings, smashed instruments, and musicians suffering massive myocardial infarctions mid-measure. The stage is a colosseum of merciless precision; panic only ever produces sour notes.\"\n\n\"Sour notes?\" Standing by the bookshelves, Pei Yi'an let out a soft, freezing chuckle.\n\nHe had not taken a seat; instead, he paced before the mahogany library like an unfeeling inspection instrument. His clinical gaze swept past framed photographs with heads of state and musical legends, locking with surgical exactitude onto a microscopic flesh-toned silver hook tucked behind He Lingfeng's right ear.\n\n\"Director He, your right auditory nerve has undergone complete necrosis; you rely entirely on a Swiss-manufactured high-precision bone-conduction hearing aid.\" Hands thrust in his trench coat pockets, Pei Yi'an pivoted, his gaze sharp as a surgical scalpel. \"The core gear train of this hearing aid operates on dual-axis micro-hairsprings—a patented design derived directly from Maurice Stein's 1934 'Brass Micro-Resonance Otoscope' custom-built for high-concession elites.\"\n\nIn that split second, the knuckles of He Lingfeng's hand cradling the tumbler locked with rigid, momentary paralysis.\n\n\"You possess a formidable grasp of mechanical engineering, young pathologist.\" He Lingfeng raised his heavy eyelids, his gaze dark as midnight.\n\n\"I hold zero interest in mechanical engineering; I am interested solely in human pathology.\" Pei Yi'an strode back to the desk, planting both hands firmly on the polished wood and leaning forward, his towering clinical presence instantly suffocating the desktop. \"Thirty years ago, the youngest Associate Chief of Otolaryngology at the Municipal Hospital was secretly scrubbed from the registry and vanished off the face of the earth on the very night Dr. Lin Qingyuan was murdered—all because he refused to falsify 'auditory restoration metrics' on Lu Chongshan's illicit neuroblocking drug trials.\"\n\nPei Yi'an stared into He Lingfeng's clouded yet cavernous eyes, peeling away the final veneer syllable by syllable:\n\n\"The young surgeon whose records were wiped clean was never named He Lingfeng; his birth name was Lin Qinghuai—the paternal half-brother of Dr. Lin Qingyuan, and the biological uncle of the late Lin Huaiyuan!\"\n\n\"What?!\" Old Zhou shuddered violently, his right palm snapping instinctively down onto his service sidearm. \"Director He... you're Lin Qingyuan's younger brother?! Then all of this... this entire string of serial butcheries, is a blood vendetta orchestrated by you?!\"\n\n\"Old Zhou, stand down.\" Pei Yi'an didn't even turn his head, his tone flat as ice. \"He is not the Ferryman. If he were the maestro conducting tonight's massacre, the bone-conduction apparatus anchored behind his right ear would not have emitted three abnormal high-frequency feedback squeals exceeding eighty decibels in the last sixty seconds.\"\n\nExtending his gloved right hand, Pei Yi'an reached out like lightning toward He Lingfeng's ear, his index finger depressing a rice-grain-sized micro-switch concealed behind the hook!\n\n*Screeech—*\n\nA blast of harsh electronic feedback erupted from the hearing aid's micro-transducer, followed immediately by a chilled, impeccably cultured voice processed through multi-tier frequency modulators:\n\n*\"Dr. Lin Qinghuai, or rather, the exalted Maestro He. Your time grows exceedingly short. One hundred and ninety minutes remain until eight o'clock tonight. If you fail to mount the podium and conduct Wen Xueqing with that finger-bone bow, your daughter studying at the Conservatoire de Genève will, within the very same second, receive a human cardiac specimen sutured in pure silver wire.\"*\n\nThe transmission severed abruptly in a static burst.\n\nOld Zhou sucked in a harsh breath, blue veins bulging along his temples: \"Bastard! That son of a bitch is using Director He's daughter to force him onto that stage as an executioner's puppet!\"\n\n\"Lin Qingyuan was my elder brother; he guarded the sacred oath of medicine until his final breath.\" He Lingfeng closed his eyes as two muddy tears tracked down his deeply furrowed cheeks, aging twenty years in the span of a heartbeat. \"Thirty years ago I fled to Europe, assumed a pseudonym, and turned to conducting, believing the sanctity of music could wash clean the humiliation and blood the Lu family inflicted upon our bloodline. But the demon never released his grip... he tracked me down, forcing me to serve as the living metronome for this slaughter!\"\n\n\"Wen Xueqing's forearm flexors are locked in violent spasms; she can't play the Chaconne to save her life.\" Old Zhou paced in frantic circles. \"EOD stated that if the music halts for over three seconds, the chemical gas beneath 1,200 seats will detonate into a fuel-air inferno! Canceling the concert means death, yet letting the curtain rise means death all the same!\"\n\n\"She doesn't need to cancel, nor does she need to complete the entire composition.\"\n\nTurning around, Pei Yi'an calmly unzipped his forensic field kit.\n\nFrom the interior foam slots, he extracted a precision micro-syringe brimming with clear liquid and a sealed sterile pack of ten-centimeter medical acupuncture needles.\n\n\"Wen Xueqing's trauma is classic post-traumatic psychogenic hypertonia, not organic neuropathology.\" A pure, crystalline flame of intellect ignited behind Pei Yi'an's spectacles. \"Utilizing high-purity mecobalamin paired with local micro-dose neural blockade, I can abolish the pathological tremors of her radial and median nerves in thirty seconds, restoring at least two hours of flawless kinetic muscle memory.\"\n\n\"And what happens after that?\" Old Zhou's eyes widened. \"Even if she executes the opening movements, when the piece ends, do you expect the explosives to magically vanish?!\"\n\n\"The complete Chaconne spans thirteen to fifteen minutes, comprising sixty-four breathtakingly intricate variations.\" Calibrating the needle against the light, Pei Yi'an expelled a single translucent droplet from the tip. \"And at the master ventilation dampers, EOD requires precisely fifteen minutes to saturate the conduits with dry ice and short-circuit the electrical firing arcs.\"\n\nTurning slightly, Pei Yi'an addressed the ashen He Lingfeng and the battle-hardened Old Zhou:\n\n\"There will be no hysteria on that stage tonight. Wen Xueqing will bow her instrument, Maestro He will command the podium, while Old Zhou and I...\"\n\nPei Yi'an nudged his spectacles, his thin lips curling into a blade-sharp, lethally calm smile:\n\n\"Before the final cadence descends in the thirteenth minute, we will follow the reverse telemetry of that transmitter, and drag the Ferryman holding the detonator straight out of the auditorium shadows!\""},{"id":11,"rawContent":"# 第十一章：鐘樓齒輪與失蹤名單\n\n傍晚六點十分，天色已被濃稠如墨的暴雨徹底吞噬。\n\n距離濱江大劇院那場生死未卜的八點音樂會，僅剩下最後一百一十分鐘。\n\n老桑塔納警車衝過老城區積水過膝的青石板路，一個急剎停在舊租界最深處的「鐘樓弄」盡頭。在雨幕狂暴的沖刷下，一座建於一九二二年的哥德式紅磚鐘樓巍然聳立在老洋房廢墟之中，四面直徑三米的巨大羅馬字鐘盤在閃電照耀下，宛如四隻冷漠俯瞰人間的白色巨眼。\n\n「這鬼地方，我當片警那會兒就聽說要拆遷，結果拆了三十年，這座破鐘樓倒比老子還能熬。」老周推開車門，小心翼翼地護著他那隻粉紅色的保溫杯，另一手高高舉著防爆強光手電筒，「小蘇，你確定那把骨弓上的銜尾蛇微型黃銅卡榫，是從這條弄堂裡流出去的？」\n\n後座上的蘇棠頂著一台加固軍用筆記型電腦，指尖飛快敲擊：「百分之百確定！我比對了全市所有具備五軸聯動激光微雕機床的工坊，整座濱江市只有這間『斯坦古董鐘錶修復所』具備在零點一毫米指骨上進行微米級冷光雕刻的精度！」\n\n三人踩著泥水穿過斑駁的鑄鐵大門，推開了鐘樓底層那扇厚重的櫟木大門。\n\n「鈴鐺——」\n\n門框上的銅鈴發出一聲清脆悠遠的輕鳴。當大門在身後合攏的瞬間，外界震耳欲聾的狂風暴雨聲竟被奇蹟般地完全隔絕。\n\n展現在眼前的，是一座令人屏息的「時間迷宮」。\n\n整座足有三層樓挑高的挑空大廳內，懸掛並陳列著數百座來自世界各地的古董鐘錶——文藝復興時期的重錘鐘、十八世紀的鎏金琺瑯自鳴鐘、龐大如怪獸般的工業水銀擒縱輪，以及數以萬計在黑暗中瘋狂咬合的黃銅齒輪。\n\n「滴答……滴答……喀嗒……喀嗒……」\n\n數百道頻率各異、節奏不一的機械撞擊聲在大廳內交織共鳴，宛如一整座機械叢林在整齊劃一地吞吐著呼吸。\n\n「進了這屋子，老子怎麼覺得連心跳都被這群破鐘給帶偏了？」老周揉了揉胸口，忍不住打了個寒顫，「小裴，這算不算心律失常？」\n\n「客觀來說，這屬於聲學節律同頻現象，常見於神經系統對外界高密度重複聲學刺激的被動適應。」裴以安收起黑傘，目光在無數旋轉的齒輪陰影中穿行，「時間本質上只是熱力學熵增的量度標尺，而兇手卻試圖用精密機械在屍體上將熵增逆轉——這是一種極致自負的病態哲學。」\n\n「年輕人，你說得很有見地。」\n\n一道沙啞蒼老、彷彿齒輪銹蝕般的聲音，毫無徵兆地從大廳深處的維修工作台後方響起。\n\n煤油燈的微弱黃光下，一個身穿灰布圍裙、戴著雙目放大鏡的駝背老人緩緩直起腰。他的左眼幾乎完全失明，眼眶深陷，右手握著一把極細的修錶鑷子，整個人枯瘦得像是一具披著粗布的活動骨架。\n\n「我是市局刑偵支隊周成林，老人家，這間修復所就您一個人？」老周亮出警官證，眼神瞬間變得無比銳利。\n\n「斯坦大師六十年前就死在集中營了，這座鐘樓裡，向來只有我和這些不會說話的指針。」老人摘下放大鏡，用渾濁的右眼打量著三人，最後目光死死定格在裴以安風衣口袋露出的那支純銀鑷子上，「你身上有福馬林的味道……還有死人的骨屑味。你是個剖開皮囊的人。」\n\n裴以安上前一步，從證物袋中取出那張從青銅雕像第四肋骨上拓印下來的「D-E-A-D」五線譜照片，以及那張銜尾蛇卡榫的微距特寫。\n\n「一九三四年莫里斯·斯坦出廠的雙軸游絲微調齒輪，配以零點零二毫米的冷光激光微雕。」裴以安冷冷地注視著老人，「這座城市裡，能做出這種機關的只有這間屋子。我要看三十年前這間工作室的所有學徒名冊與委託記錄。」\n\n老人枯瘦的手指輕輕拂過照片上的銜尾蛇圖騰，身形猛然劇烈震顫了一下。\n\n「這不是委託……這是三十年前逃走的那個孩子……」老人的喉嚨裡發出一陣風箱般的哮喘聲，眼角泛起渾濁的淚光，「他回來了……他真的拿著手術刀和發條回來了……」\n\n「哪個孩子？！叫什麼名字？！」老周一把按住老人的肩膀。\n\n老人顫巍巍地轉身，從工作台最底層那隻包鐵的樟木箱裡，捧出了一本被蟲蛀斑斑的厚重牛皮登記冊。冊子的紙張早已發脆泛黃，扉頁上赫然印著一九九四年的燙金字樣。\n\n老周一把翻開冊子，在泛黃的紙頁深處，赫然夾著一張三十年前市立醫院的實習醫師證明與領養協議！\n\n協議上的照片，是一個眼神陰鬱、面容清秀的十四歲少年。而在他的監護人簽名欄與學徒姓名欄上，赫然寫著兩個重重砸進老周心頭的名字：\n\n**受資助實習學徒：秦墨（Qin Mo）。**\n\n**原委託擔保人：濱江市立醫院病理科主任——林清源！**\n\n「秦墨？！」老周倒吸一口涼氣，腦海中記憶的碎片如風暴般狂暴拼合，「三十年前林清源博士在二號乾塢遇害前收養的那個醫學神童兼機械天才？！當年林博士死後，這個十四歲的孩子就人間蒸發了……所有人都以為他跳江殉師了！」\n\n「他沒有死。」裴以安修長的指尖滑過登記冊最後一頁的備註欄，那裡赫然用深藍色墨水寫著一行字：\n\n*「以骨為弦，以血為墨；三十年後，鐘聲再起時，審判濱江。」*\n\n就在這一瞬間，整座鐘樓三層頂端的巨型齒輪室內，突然傳來了一陣令人頭皮發麻的低頻電磁蜂鳴聲！\n\n「周隊！裴老師！」守在門口筆記型電腦旁的蘇棠突然爆發出一聲驚恐的尖叫，「信號！我們頭頂上的鐘樓發射塔突然對外發射了高頻微波信號！接收端……接收端正是濱江大劇院地下的一千二百個化學炸藥繼電器！」\n\n老周與裴以安同時拔腿衝上鐵鑄旋轉樓梯，狂奔向鐘樓最高層的鐘機房！\n\n當兩人撞開塵封的頂層鐵門時，眼前的一幕讓身經百戰的老刑警整個人僵死在原地——\n\n在整座高達四米的巨型青銅機械鐘芯正中央，一座原本懸掛重錘的滑輪上，赫然被一根鋼絲吊著一台正在倒計時的數位液晶定時器！\n\n定時器的液晶屏上，猩紅的數字正以毫秒級的速度瘋狂流逝：\n\n**「01 : 15 : 22」——距離晚間八點整，只剩最後一小時十五分鐘！**\n\n更致命的是，那台定時器的外殼上，赫然插著一隻由十三根人體橈骨與尺骨拼裝而成的巨大機械撥叉，死死卡在鐘樓每逢整點敲響的百噸青銅大鐘的傳動齒輪之中！\n\n裴以安仰頭看著那座巨大的骨骼齒輪機關，鏡片後那雙深邃的眼眸中，倒映著猩紅倒計時冰冷刺目的光芒：\n\n「這座鐘樓的大鐘，根本不是用來報時的。」\n\n裴以安聲音極輕，卻像一道淬毒的冰凌扎進空氣：\n\n「八點鐘一到，鐘樓的大鐘敲響，聲波與無線電信號將會同時引爆大劇院。擺渡人不是要坐在觀眾席裡看戲……他是在這座三十年前的鐘樓頂上，親手敲響全城的喪鐘！」","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 11: Clocktower Gears & The Missing Register\n\nAt 6:10 in the evening, the sky had been thoroughly swallowed by a downpour as thick and viscous as ink.\n\nBarely one hundred and ten minutes remained before the curtain rose upon the mortal concert at the Binjiang Grand Theatre at eight sharp.\n\nThe aged Santana cruiser ploughed through floodwaters submerging the cobblestones past the knees in the historic quarter, screeching to an emergency halt at the terminus of \"Clocktower Alley\" in the deepest heart of the old concession. Beneath the furious scour of the tempest, a Gothic red-brick clocktower erected in 1922 towered imposingly amidst the ruins of colonial mansions, its four colossal Roman numeral dials—each three meters across—gleaming beneath flashes of lightning like four giant, unblinking white eyes peering cold and indifferent down upon the world.\n\n\"This godforsaken swamp—back when I was a beat cop thirty years ago, they swore it was slated for demolition. Thirty years later, this dilapidated clocktower has outlived my entire youth.\" Old Zhou shoved open the door, carefully shielding his pink smart thermos with one arm while hoisting a tactical searchlight high with the other. \"Little Su, are you certain that miniature ouroboros brass slide on the bone bow traced back to this alley?\"\n\nIn the rear seat, Su Tang balanced a ruggedized military laptop upon her knees, her fingers typing at frantic speed: \"A hundred percent certain! I ran cross-checks against every five-axis CNC laser micro-engraving workshop in the municipality. In the whole of Binjiang, only this 'Stein Antique Horology Restoration Studio' commands the precision to execute micro-metric cold-laser incisions upon 0.1-millimeter phalanges!\"\n\nSloshing through slurry, the three crossed the mottled cast-iron gates and hauled open the massive oak portal at the base of the clocktower.\n\n*Cling-clang—*\n\nThe brass bell affixed to the lintel chimed with crisp, lingering resonance. The instant the heavy leaf swung shut behind them, the deafening tempest raging outside was miraculous cut off in an eyeblink.\n\nUnfolding before their eyes was an awe-inspiring \"labyrinth of time.\"\n\nAcross a cavernous three-story open atrium, hundreds of antique clocks and mechanical timepieces gathered from around the globe hung from the masonry and lined the display cases—Renaissance pendulum regulators, eighteenth-century gilded enamel chimes, monstrous industrial mercury escapements, and tens of thousands of raw brass gear trains interlocking in furious, frantic precision within the gloom.\n\n*Tick-tock... tick-tock... clack-clack... clack-clack...*\n\nHundreds of mechanical impacts differing in frequency and cadence intertwined throughout the hall, humming like an entire synthetic jungle inhaling and exhaling in disciplined synchronization.\n\n\"Walking into this tomb, why do I feel like my own ticker is getting dragged out of rhythm by these damned clocks?\" Old Zhou rubbed his chest, suppressing an involuntary shiver. \"Little Pei, does this count as cardiac arrhythmia?\"\n\n\"Objectively speaking, this constitutes acoustic frequency-following response—a common passive neurological adaptation to high-density, repetitive external sonic stimuli.\" Folding his black umbrella, Pei Yi'an paced through the shadows of countless whirling gears. \"Time is fundamentally merely the physical measurement of thermodynamic entropy increasing; yet the perpetrator attempts through precision machinery to reverse entropy across a corpse—an act of supreme, pathological arrogance.\"\n\n\"Young man, you speak with profound insight.\"\n\nA gravelly, ancient voice—resembling the rasp of oxidized gear teeth—drifted without warning from behind the workbench deep in the hall.\n\nBeneath the dim yellow pool of a kerosene lamp, a hunchbacked elder in a canvas apron and binocular loupes slowly straightened his spine. His left eye was entirely blind, the socket sunken, while his withered right hand clutched an ultra-fine watchmaker's tweezers, resembling an animated skeleton draped in rough cloth.\n\n\"Municipal Criminal Investigation Detachment, Captain Zhou Chenglin. Old gentleman, are you the sole occupant of this workshop?\" Flashing his police credentials, Old Zhou's eyes turned razor-sharp in an instant.\n\n\"Master Stein perished in the camps sixty years ago; within this tower, there have only ever been myself and these hands that never speak.\" Removing his loupes, the elder scrutinized the three with his clouded right eye, his gaze arresting rigidly upon the solid-silver dissecting forceps protruding from Pei Yi'an's trench coat breast pocket. \"You carry the scent of formalin... and the dust of human bone. You are one who cuts away the mortal skin.\"\n\nStepping forward, Pei Yi'an retrieved from his evidence pouch the polarized macro-photographs of the \"D-E-A-D\" musical staff from the bronze statue's fourth rib, along with extreme close-ups of the ouroboros brass slide.\n\n\"A 1934 Maurice Stein dual-axis hairspring micro-regulation gear train, combined with 0.02-millimeter cold-laser micro-engraving.\" Pei Yi'an fixed his gaze upon the old watchmaker with glacial intensity. \"Across this entire metropolis, only this room possesses the capability to forge such mechanisms. I want to inspect all apprentice rosters and client ledgers belonging to this studio from thirty years ago.\"\n\nThe elder's withered fingertips traced the ouroboros totem upon the glossy paper, his frail frame shuddering with sudden violence.\n\n\"This was no commission... this was that boy who fled thirty years ago...\" A rattling wheeze like a rusted bellows scraped from the elder's throat, cloudy tears welling in the corners of his eyes. \"He returned... he truly came back carrying scalpels and clockwork springs...\"\n\n\"Which boy?! What was his name?!\" Old Zhou clamped a hand onto the watchmaker's shoulder.\n\nTrembling, the elder turned and hauled an iron-bound camphor chest from beneath the lowest tier of the workbench, lifting out a heavy, moth-eaten cowhide ledger. The parchment leaves were brittle and yellowed, the title page stamped with gilded lettering from 1994.\n\nOld Zhou threw the volume open. Tucked between the brittle pages was an official hospital internship credential and an adoption agreement from thirty years ago!\n\nGlaring out from the faded photograph was a fourteen-year-old youth with a melancholy gaze and refined, delicate features. And upon the legal guardian and apprentice signature lines were inscribed two names that struck Old Zhou's chest like leaden cannonballs:\n\n**Sponsored Apprentice: Qin Mo.**\n\n**Original Sponsoring Guardian: Chief of Pathology, Binjiang Municipal Hospital—Dr. Lin Qingyuan!**\n\n\"Qin Mo?!\" Old Zhou gasped, shattered fragments of thirty-year-old memory colliding like a hurricane within his mind. \"The medical prodigy and mechanical genius Dr. Lin Qingyuan took in right before he was murdered in Dry Dock Number Two?! When Dr. Lin was killed, that fourteen-year-old boy vanished into thin air... everyone assumed he had jumped into the river to follow his master!\"\n\n\"He never died.\" Pei Yi'an's slender fingers glided across the margin of the ledger's final page, where a line of dark-blue fountain pen ink remained:\n\n*\"Bones for strings, blood for ink; thirty years hence, when the chimes toll again, judgment shall fall upon Binjiang.\"*\n\nAt that exact second, from within the colossal gear room atop the clocktower's third story, an ear-splitting, low-frequency electromagnetic whine tore through the rafters!\n\n\"Captain Zhou! Teacher Pei!\" Su Tang—stationed beside her laptop near the entry—let out a terrified shriek. \"A signal! The transmission antenna above our heads just emitted a high-frequency microwave pulse! The receiver... the receiver is locked onto the 1,200 chemical relay detonators under the seats at the Grand Theatre!\"\n\nUnholstering their weapons, Old Zhou and Pei Yi'an sprinted up the spiral cast-iron staircase, charging headlong into the clockwork machinery chamber at the summit of the tower!\n\nAs they kicked open the dust-encrusted iron bulkhead, the spectacle awaiting them arrested the battle-hardened detective dead in his tracks—\n\nIn the center of the four-meter-tall monumental bronze clock escapement, suspended from the cable originally carrying the counterweight, hung a digital countdown timer!\n\nAcross the timer's glowing LCD panel, crimson digits were bleeding away at millisecond velocity:\n\n**\"01 : 15 : 22\" — Exactly one hour and fifteen minutes remained until eight o'clock sharp!**\n\nFar more fatal, bolted onto the timer's casing was a massive mechanical pallet fork assembled from thirteen human radius and ulna bones, wedged immovably into the drive gears of the hundred-ton bronze municipal bell that tolled the top of every hour!\n\nLooking up into the colossal skeletal clockwork mechanism, the crimson glare of the countdown mirrored cold and blinding in Pei Yi'an's glasses:\n\n\"This municipal bell was never engineered to tell time.\"\n\nPei Yi'an's voice was whisper-soft, yet it drove into the air like a poisoned needle:\n\n\"The moment eight o'clock strikes, the bell will toll, and the acoustic shockwave paired with the microwave pulse will detonate the Grand Theatre simultaneously. The Ferryman never planned to sit in the audience watching the show... he stands atop this thirty-year-old clocktower, preparing to toll the death knell for the entire city with his own hands!\""},{"id":12,"rawContent":"# 第十二章：舊水管深處的殘骸密碼\n\n鐘樓頂層的狂風穿透百葉窗欞，發出猶如厲鬼啼哭般的尖嘯。\n\n機械鐘芯正中央，猩紅的數位定時器瘋狂跳動著，數字已赫然變成了「01 : 04 : 18」。距離八點整的濱江大劇院交響音樂會，僅剩最後六十四分鐘。\n\n「老子現在就上去把那幾根破骨頭砸碎，剪斷引線！」老周滿臉煞氣，從腰間拔出警用多功能戰術鉗，邁步就要跨過那座由數以萬計黃銅齒輪咬合而成的運轉基座。\n\n「周隊，如果你想讓這座鐘樓連同我們三個在一微秒內化為焦炭，並且提前六十分鐘引爆大劇院，你可以儘管剪下去。」\n\n裴以安冰冷的聲音像一針極效鎮靜劑，硬生生將老周釘在了半空中。\n\n年輕法醫蹲下身，手電筒的光束聚成一束筆直的冷光，落在定時器兩側那十三根懸空的橈骨與尺骨上。\n\n「你看骨骼兩端的骨骺線連接處。」裴以安的長鑷子輕輕懸停在一根尺骨上方三毫米處，「這十三根骨骼被挖空了骨髓腔，裡面灌注了水銀與高敏光阻化學試劑，並以極微細的鍍銀銅絲串聯成一組動態扭力平衡傳感器。只要外力破壞超過零點五牛頓，或者剪斷任何一根線路導致電位失衡，底部的壓電陶瓷撞針就會立刻釋放高壓微波脈衝。」\n\n老周額頭滲出豆大的冷汗，默默將戰術鉗塞回了皮套，順手抓起粉紅色保溫杯灌了一大口溫水：「這小畜生到底是跟誰學的？三十年前市立醫院的病理科還教這手炸彈手藝？」\n\n「這不是病理學，這是鐘錶機械工藝、神經生理學與破壞工程學的畸形結合體。」裴以安目光如刀，沿著定時器後方那幾根極粗的黑色同軸電纜向下審視，「而且，這裡根本不是信號發射源。」\n\n「什麼？！」守在旋轉樓梯口的蘇棠猛地抬起頭，抱著軍用電腦失聲驚呼，「裴老師說得沒錯！我的頻譜儀剛剛捕捉到了電磁回波！頂樓這個只是被動轉發天線和諧振開關，真正的微波控制中繼站……在我們腳底下！在鐘樓的最底層地下深處！」\n\n三人片刻不敢耽擱，順著狹窄逼仄的生鏽鑄鐵旋轉梯狂奔而下，直撲鐘樓地下一層早已荒廢數十年的老鍋爐房。\n\n鍋爐房內積滿了齊膝深的黑色煤渣泥水，空氣中瀰漫著濃烈的硫磺味與刺鼻的鐵鏽臭氣。在角落一座倒塌的重油鍋爐後方，一塊生鐵鑄造的圓形重型井蓋被斜斜掀開了一道半米寬的縫隙，露出黑洞洞的垂直豎井。\n\n「這是一九二二年租界當局修建的德式地下排水幹渠。」蘇棠用戰術平板迅速調出老城區市政管網圖，「直徑兩米五，全長三點八公里，正好從鐘樓弄地下穿過老港區，最後直通濱江大劇院地下的雨水調蓄池！」\n\n「真他娘的是個老鼠洞。」老周罵了一句，擰亮頭燈，第一個抓住濕滑冰冷的鐵爬梯滑進了深淵，「小蘇留在上面負責通訊協調，小裴，跟緊我！要是下面有埋伏，老子拿防暴盾給你擋著！」\n\n裴以安一言不發，將大衣下擺紮緊在腰間，手提銀色勘查箱，身手俐落地攀梯而下。\n\n管渠深處的水流湍急而冰冷，黑濁的雨水已經漫到了兩人的大腿根部，空氣中瀰漫著沼氣與重金屬廢水混雜的作嘔氣味。\n\n「小裴，等這案子結了，你必須給我寫一份公傷申請。」老周一邊深一腳淺一腳地在濕滑的磚砌管壁間逆流摸索，一邊咬牙切齒，「就寫『老刑警涉險橫渡百年化糞池，造成嚴重精神與褲管創傷』。」\n\n「客觀而言，這裡主要成分是天然雨水沉積物與瀝青微粒，糞大腸桿菌濃度尚在安全閾值內。」裴以安打著防水紫外線手電筒，冷淡地回應，「但如果你的保溫杯不慎掉進水裡，我建議你立即對其進行高壓蒸汽滅菌或者乾脆遺棄。」\n\n老周聞言，頓時像護崽的母雞一樣把保溫杯死死掖進防彈背心裡。\n\n兩人沿著管壁上方那根被新鮮絕緣膠帶固定住的黑色信號電纜，在黑暗的地下水迷宮中前行了約三百米。\n\n在穿過一道生鏽的重力水閘門後，眼前的景象豁然開朗。\n\n這是一處早已乾涸廢棄的拱頂調蓄分水室，四面紅磚牆壁上掛滿了慘白的蛛網與硝石結晶。而在分水室中央的一座平坦水泥平台上，赫然亮著一盞便攜式充電日光燈。\n\n白慘慘的燈光下，擺放著一張用舊木門板臨時搭成的手術工作台。\n\n「周隊，看那裡。」裴以安的瞳孔驟然收縮。\n\n在手術台正中央，沒有血肉，只有一座被固定在黃銅三腳架上的完整人體頭骨！\n\n那座頭骨的下頜骨被精密地固定在一個音叉式機械諧振器上，而在頭骨的顱頂骨與額骨交界處，赫然用微型鑽頭刻滿了密密麻麻的數字矩陣與波形符號。\n\n「又是骨頭……這瘋子難道把整座濱江市都當成了他的骨科陳列室？！」老周端著手槍警惕地環視四周，靴底在水泥地上踩出黏膩的水聲，「人呢？秦墨不在這裡！」\n\n「他二十分鐘前剛離開。」裴以安走上前，指尖輕輕觸碰日光燈的散熱鋁片，「燈體餘溫大約攝氏四十二度，地面上的鞋印泥漿尚未脫水固化。」\n\n他的目光迅速落在那具頭骨上，眼神凝重無比：「這不是受害者的骨頭。從矢狀縫閉合程度、蝶頂縫癒合狀態以及磨損的臼齒特徵來看，這是一位年齡在五十五歲左右的成年男性，死亡時間……整整三十年。」\n\n老周的呼吸猛地停滯了：「五十五歲……三十年前……這具頭骨……難道是林清源博士？！」\n\n「頭骨枕骨大孔處有一處直徑八毫米的鈍器粉碎性凹陷骨折，邊緣伴有生前出血浸潤反應。」裴以安戴上乳膠手套，用探針輕輕探入枕骨裂隙，「這才是林清源的真正死因——他根本不是三十年前官方通報的『乾塢失足溺水』，而是在落水前被人從背後用重錘擊碎了枕骨！」\n\n「三十年前……有人在乾塢滅了林博士的口，偽裝成意外，逼得十四歲的秦墨流亡三十年。」老周的雙手因憤怒而微微顫抖，「秦墨挖出了他導師的頭骨……他到底要用這顆頭骨做什麼？！」\n\n「看牙齒。」裴以安調整放大鏡焦距，強光直射在頭骨的上頜第一前磨牙與犬齒的琺瑯質上。\n\n在堅硬無比的牙齒琺瑯質表面，赫然被用微米激光刻著一排極小的頻率參數：**【432 Hz - Resonance Override : 0x7F9A】**。\n\n「432赫茲……」裴以安喃喃自語，「這是莫札特時代的古典音樂基準頻率，也是這具頭骨顱骨板障與黃銅諧振器的固有物理共振頻率。」\n\n「什麼意思？小裴你快說人話！我們只剩下四十分鐘了！」老周急得直跺腳。\n\n「秦墨故意把頭骨留在這裡，作為這座微波控制網絡的『終極安全密鑰』。」裴以安飛快地從箱子裡取出微型音叉與音頻發生器，「他知道警察遲早會追到這裡。但全市只有能看懂骨骼微觀結構的法醫，才能從他導師的牙齒上讀出這個頻率矩陣，從而安全閉鎖微波發射信號！」\n\n「這小子……他是在逼你隔空替他給林博士完成最後一場法醫鑒定！」老周恍然大悟。\n\n裴以安沒有回答，他的眼神專注到了極致，手指精準調校著音頻發生器的旋鈕。\n\n「432.05赫茲……相位角180度……」\n\n當音頻探針接觸到頭骨顳骨鱗部的瞬間，整座頭骨與下方的黃銅諧振器突然發出了一聲清亮剔透的共鳴嗡鳴！\n\n「滴——」\n\n連接著頭骨後方的信號發射模組上，那顆瘋狂閃爍的猩紅指示燈，在一聲清脆的繼電器跳閘聲中，驟然變成了穩定的幽綠色！\n\n地面上方同時傳來蘇棠耳麥裡興奮得帶著哭腔的吶喊：「周隊！成功了！鐘樓頂樓的微波繼電器被強制閉鎖了！大劇院地下的爆炸觸發鏈條被成功切斷了！」\n\n老周長長吐出一口濁氣，整個人幾乎脫力般靠在冰冷的磚牆上：「他娘的……總算保住那群聽交響樂的觀眾了……」\n\n「還沒有。」裴以安的聲音依舊冷冽得像冰。\n\n他用手電筒照向分水室另一端通往大劇院地下調蓄池的維修鐵柵欄。\n\n那道原本緊鎖的鐵柵門，鎖扣已被液壓鉗整齊剪斷，地上留著一串清晰帶泥的水漬腳印，腳印旁還遺落著一張濕漉漉的燙金邀請函——\n\n**【濱江大劇院·今晚八點·首席小提琴獨奏特邀嘉賓座席】**。\n\n「他根本沒打算靠定時炸彈引爆。」裴以安盯著那張邀請函，字字如刀，「微波炸彈只是牽制警力的幌子。真正的審判……他要親自走上大劇院的舞台，在眾目睽睽之下親手執行！」\n\n「走！」老周一拉槍栓，眼中寒芒暴漲，「老子倒要看看，這隻躲了三十年的幽靈，今晚到底要在舞台上拉什麼調子！」","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 12: Debris Ciphers Deep in Old Drainage\n\nGales atop the clocktower pierced through the louvered shutters, howling like the shrieks of vengeful specters.\n\nAt the dead center of the mechanical movement, the crimson digital timer pulsed feverishly, its figures now glaring at \"01 : 04 : 18.\" Barely sixty-four minutes remained before the symphony concert commenced at eight sharp at the Binjiang Grand Theatre.\n\n\"I'm climbing up there right now to smash those damn bones and sever the detonator wires!\" Old Zhou growled ferociously, yanking a tactical multi-tool from his belt and preparing to step across the spinning bed of tens of thousands of interlocking brass gear trains.\n\n\"Captain Zhou, if your objective is to reduce this clocktower and the three of us into cinders within a single microsecond—and detonate the Grand Theatre sixty minutes ahead of schedule—by all means, make the cut.\"\n\nPei Yi'an's glacial tone acted like a potent sedative, freezing Old Zhou rigidly mid-stride.\n\nThe young forensic pathologist crouched, focusing his flashlight into a crisp beam of cold luminescence that settled upon the thirteen suspended radii and ulnae flanking the timer.\n\n\"Observe the epiphyseal junctions at both ends of the bones,\" Pei Yi'an said, hovering his long forceps three millimeters above an ulna. \"The medullary cavities of these thirteen bones have been hollowed out and injected with mercury and highly photosensitive chemical reagents, daisy-chained with ultra-fine silvered copper filaments into a dynamic torque balance sensor. The moment any external tampering exceeds 0.5 Newtons, or any wire is snipped to cause a potential imbalance, the piezoelectric ceramic striker at the base will instantly unleash a high-voltage microwave pulse.\"\n\nCold sweat beaded on Old Zhou's forehead as he silently holstered his tactical pliers, promptly unscrewing his pink thermos to gulp a mouthful of warm water. \"Who in the hell taught that brat this craft? Did Municipal Hospital's pathology department thirty years ago offer electives in bomb-making?\"\n\n\"This is not pathology; this is a monstrous hybridization of horological engineering, neurophysiology, and demolition dynamics.\" Pei Yi'an's gaze cut like a scalpel, tracing the heavy black coaxial cables running down from behind the timer. \"Furthermore, this is not the origin of the transmission.\"\n\n\"What?!\" Su Tang, perched at the entrance of the spiral staircase hugging her military laptop, gasped aloud. \"Teacher Pei is spot on! My spectrum analyzer just registered electromagnetic echo returns! The apparatus on the top floor is merely a passive repeater antenna and resonant switch. The master microwave control station... is beneath our feet! Deep within the subterranean foundations of this tower!\"\n\nWasting not a second, the trio bounded down the cramped, rusted cast-iron spiral staircase, heading straight for the abandoned boiler room in the clocktower's subterranean basement.\n\nThe boiler room was flooded knee-deep with black coal-slurry runoff, the stagnant air heavy with sulfur fumes and pungent ferric rot. Behind a collapsed heavy-oil boiler in the corner, a massive cast-iron manhole cover had been levered askew by half a meter, revealing a gaping vertical shaft descending into pitch blackness.\n\n\"This is a German-engineered municipal storm conduit constructed by concession authorities in 1922,\" Su Tang reported, pulling up the historic municipal blueprints on her tactical tablet. \"Two and a half meters in diameter and 3.8 kilometers in total length, it cuts directly beneath Clocktower Alley through the old docklands, culminating directly into the stormwater retention basin beneath the Binjiang Grand Theatre!\"\n\n\"A bloody rat hole if I ever saw one,\" Old Zhou cursed under his breath, clicking on his headlamp. He was the first to grab the slimy, icy rungs of the iron ladder and drop into the abyss. \"Little Su, remain up top to coordinate communications. Little Pei, stay glued to my six! If there's an ambush down there, I'll take the brunt with my riot shield!\"\n\nWithout a word, Pei Yi'an hitched his trench coat hem into his belt, grabbed his silver forensic field kit, and descended the ladder with crisp, practiced agility.\n\nDeep inside the conduit, the underground surge churned swift and freezing, the turbid, soot-stained flood reaching their upper thighs, while the stench of marsh gas and industrial runoff induced immediate nausea.\n\n\"Little Pei, once this case wraps, you're drafting a workman's comp claim for me,\" Old Zhou grunted through gritted teeth, trudging upstream along the slimy brick culvert. \"Write down: 'Senior detective braved century-old cesspool in line of duty, suffering acute psychological trauma and catastrophic loss of trousers.'\"\n\n\"Objectively speaking, the dominant constituents here are stormwater sediments and asphalt particulates; fecal coliform counts remain within acceptable thresholds,\" Pei Yi'an remarked dispassionately under his waterproof UV light. \"However, should your thermos tumble into this water, I recommend immediate autoclave sterilization, if not outright disposal.\"\n\nHearing this, Old Zhou instinctively clutched the thermos tighter against his tactical vest, guarding it like a mother hen shielding her brood.\n\nFollowing the fresh black signal cable taped along the upper brickwork, the two pushed roughly three hundred meters into the subterranean water maze.\n\nAfter squeezing past a rusted gravity sluice gate, the passage opened into a vaulted chamber.\n\nIt was a dry, long-decommissioned subterranean distribution vault, its red-brick arches draped in pale cobwebs and saltpeter efflorescence. In the middle of the chamber, atop an elevated concrete slab, a portable rechargeable fluorescent lamp shone brightly.\n\nBeneath its harsh, sterile glare sat a makeshift surgical workbench rigged from a salvaged wooden door leaf.\n\n\"Captain Zhou, look there,\" Pei Yi'an muttered, his pupils constricting sharply.\n\nIn the middle of the operating surface lay no flesh, only an intact human cranium mounted securely upon a brass tripod fixture!\n\nThe mandible of the cranium was locked into a tuning-fork mechanical resonator, while the coronal suture between the frontal and parietal bones was painstakingly micro-drilled with a dense matrix of numeric coordinates and waveform schematics.\n\n\"Bones again... Has this lunatic turned the entire municipality of Binjiang into his personal osteological gallery?!\" Old Zhou leveled his service weapon, sweeping the shadows as his boots splashed across the concrete. \"Where is he? Qin Mo isn't here!\"\n\n\"He departed approximately twenty minutes ago,\" Pei Yi'an said, stepping forward to brush the aluminum heat sink of the fluorescent lamp. \"Residual surface temperature sits around forty-two degrees Celsius, and the mud slurry within the footprints on the floor has yet to dehydrate and solidify.\"\n\nHis gaze shifted heavily onto the mounted skull, darkening with solemn gravity. \"This does not belong to a recent victim. Judging by the obliteration of the sagittal suture, sphenoparietal synchondrosis fusion, and coronal occlusal wear on the molars, this belonged to an adult male aged approximately fifty-five. Post-mortem interval... exactly thirty years.\"\n\nOld Zhou's breath hitched violently in his chest. \"Fifty-five years old... thirty years ago... This skull... Could it be Dr. Lin Qingyuan?!\"\n\n\"At the margin of the foramen magnum lies an eight-millimeter depressed comminuted fracture from blunt force trauma, exhibiting unmistakable vital ante-mortem hemorrhagic infiltration,\" Pei Yi'an said, snapping on latex gloves and probing the fissure with a sterile stylus. \"This is the true cause of Lin Qingyuan's demise—he never died of an 'accidental drowning' in Dry Dock No. 2 as officially declared; he was bludgeoned from behind with a sledgehammer prior to immersion!\"\n\n\"Thirty years ago... someone silenced Dr. Lin in the dry dock, staged it as a mishap, and forced the fourteen-year-old Qin Mo into thirty years of exile.\" Old Zhou's fists trembled with rage. \"Qin Mo exhumed his mentor's cranium... What on earth does he intend to do with it?!\"\n\n\"Look at the dentition,\" Pei Yi'an instructed, focusing his loupe as stark light flooded the enamel of the skull's maxillary first premolar and canine.\n\nEtched into the diamond-hard enamel by cold-laser ablation was a minuscule string of frequency parameters: **【432 Hz - Resonance Override : 0x7F9A】**.\n\n\"432 Hertz...\" Pei Yi'an murmured. \"The standard concert pitch from the classical era of Mozart—and the intrinsic physical resonant frequency of this diploë cranial bone structure paired with the brass resonator.\"\n\n\"What does that mean? Little Pei, speak plain human! We only have forty minutes left!\" Old Zhou pleaded, stamping his foot in agitation.\n\n\"Qin Mo deliberately stationed this cranium here as the 'ultimate fail-safe key' for the microwave detonator network,\" Pei Yi'an said, swiftly withdrawing a miniature tuning fork and frequency generator from his case. \"He knew the authorities would eventually track him here. But across this entire city, only a pathologist trained to decipher micro-skeletal architecture could extract this matrix from his mentor's teeth to safely override the transmitter!\"\n\n\"That bastard... he's compelling you from afar to perform Dr. Lin's final autopsy in his stead!\" Old Zhou gasped in realization.\n\nPei Yi'an offered no response, his focus dialed to absolute precision as his fingers adjusted the rotary dial of the audio generator.\n\n\"432.05 Hertz... Phase angle 180 degrees...\"\n\nThe instant the acoustic probe contacted the squama temporalis of the skull, the entire cranium and the brass resonator beneath hummed with crystal-clear sympathetic resonance!\n\n*Beep—*\n\nMounted behind the cranium, the frantic crimson diode on the signal transceiver snapped off with a sharp relay click, stabilizing into a solid, soothing emerald green!\n\nFrom above ground, Su Tang's voice burst through the earpiece, giddy with tearful relief: \"Captain Zhou! It worked! The microwave repeater atop the clocktower has been forced into failsafe lock! The subterranean detonation trigger chain for the Grand Theatre is severed!\"\n\nOld Zhou released a prolonged breath, leaning limply against the damp brickwork. \"Thank God... We saved those symphony-goers after all...\"\n\n\"Not yet,\" Pei Yi'an said, his tone still cold as glacial ice.\n\nHe swept his tactical beam toward the service iron grate at the far end of the vault leading directly into the Grand Theatre's drainage sump.\n\nThe padlocks securing the gate had been sheared cleanly through by hydraulic bolt-cutters. On the flagstones trailed a fresh sequence of wet, muddy footprints, beside which lay a soggy, gold-embossed invitation—\n\n**【Binjiang Grand Theatre · Tonight at 8:00 PM · Principal Violinist Solo Guest of Honor Reservation】**.\n\n\"He never intended to detonate the building from afar,\" Pei Yi'an remarked, his words sharp as a scalpel. \"The microwave bomb was merely a decoy to tie down the police force. The true execution... he plans to walk onto that stage and deliver it in full view of the world!\"\n\n\"Move!\" Old Zhou racked his slide, a fierce glint burning in his eyes. \"I want to see for myself what kind of tune this thirty-year-old ghost intends to play upon that stage tonight!\""},{"id":13,"rawContent":"# 第十三章：大劇院最後的樂章\n\n晚間七點五十分，距離八點整的開演鐘聲，只剩最後十分鐘。\n\n暴雨如注的江面之上，濱江大劇院宛如一隻橫臥在雨夜中的巨大水晶貝殼，通體由鋼化玻璃與鈦合金桁架構成的穹頂在閃電照耀下泛著冰冷刺目的銀光。\n\n劇院正門外，豪車雲集，盛裝出席的城中名流與政商權貴正踩著被雨水打濕的紅地毯魚貫而入。而在劇院地下一層陰暗潮濕的雨水調蓄池旁，一道鏽蝕的檢修鐵門被「砰」地一聲粗暴踹開。\n\n老周渾身滴著臭烘烘的黑濁泥水，褲腳捲到膝蓋上方，防彈背心裡死死護著他那隻印著褪色草莓圖案的粉紅色保溫杯，另一手緊扣著九二式手槍的保險機。\n\n「咳……咳咳！老子這輩子抓過殺人犯、端過走私窩，頭一回鑽三公里的下水道來聽高雅交響樂。」老周抹了一把臉上的雨水，警惕地掃視著後台通往樂池的通道，「小裴，你看這身打扮，門口的保安會不會直接拿防暴叉把老子叉出去？」\n\n「如果從流行病學與公共衛生角度考量，保安有充分理由對你實施強制隔離並進行全車消殺。」裴以安提著銀色勘查箱從鐵梯躍下，風衣下擺雖然濺滿了泥點，但金絲眼鏡後的目光依舊冷靜得像精密卡尺，「距離鐘樓八點報時還有九分鐘。更衣室在走廊左側第三間。」\n\n兩人避開巡邏的安保人員，疾步穿過鋪著吸音地毯的後台走廊。\n\n此時的後台亂作一團，身著黑色燕尾服與曳地晚禮服的樂手們正忙碌地調音、鬆香、整理樂譜。空氣中交織著松節油、高級香水與演出前焦慮荷爾蒙的混合氣味。\n\n「等等。」裴以安突然停下腳步，目光如手術刀般穿透更衣室半掩的門扉。\n\n更衣室內的長凳上，劇院特邀的客座首席小提琴家正昏睡在化妝台前，呼吸深沉綿長。裴以安上前翻開他的眼瞼，指尖在其頸動脈處輕輕一搭：「瞳孔對光反射遲鈍，呼氣帶有微弱的苦杏仁甜味。被注射了微量的丙泊酚靜脈麻醉劑，劑量精確到毫克級，恰好讓他昏睡三小時而不致呼吸衰竭。」\n\n而在化妝鏡前的空衣架上，原本掛著的那套訂製燕尾服，以及琴盒裡的瓜奈里名琴，早已不翼而飛。\n\n「調包了！那小畜生換上燕尾服，混進樂池了！」老周臉色驟變，拔腿就要往舞台主入口衝。\n\n「周隊，冷靜。」裴以安一把扣住老周的手腕，手勁大得驚人，「台下坐著一千八百名觀眾，前排全是市政要員與商會理事。你現在端著槍衝進去大喊有炸彈，引發的踩踏傷亡將遠遠超過一場局部爆炸。」\n\n「那你要老子怎麼辦？眼睜睜看著他把全場一千八百人送上天？！」老周咬著後槽牙，眼眶泛紅。\n\n「微波引爆鏈條已經在地下幹渠被我們徹底鎖死，他手裡沒有起爆器。」裴以安指了指那張遺落在下水道的邀請函，「這場演出的主贊助商，是楚氏生物醫藥集團的董事長楚天成——正是三十年前市立醫院病理研究所的副院長，林清源博士當年的頂頭上司。」\n\n老周身軀劇烈一震，腦中所有破碎的線索在這一秒被閃電貫通：「楚天成？！三十年前林清源遇害後，是他接管了林博士所有的生物抗癌專利，靠著這批成果下海組建了楚氏醫藥，成了濱江首富！」\n\n「林清源的頭骨上有重錘擊打的痕跡，而楚天成當年正是用這筆血染的專利完成了資本原始積累。」裴以安迅速穿上一件工作人員遺落的深色工裝外套，扣上工作證，「秦墨不是要屠殺無辜的觀眾。他要的是在楚天成人生最輝煌的榮譽授勳之夜，用林清源的骨頭，親手執行遲到了三十年的死刑。」\n\n舞台前方，清脆的預備鈴聲驟然響起。\n\n晚間七點五十八分。\n\n大劇院主音樂廳內的璀璨水晶吊燈緩緩熄滅，深藍色的聚光燈如銀瀑般灑向舞台中央。全場一千八百名觀眾掌聲雷動。\n\n在第一排正中央的貴賓包廂內，年過六旬、頭髮梳理得一絲不苟的楚天成整了整胸前閃閃發光的「城市傑出貢獻勳章」，滿面春風地向身旁的官員與名流致意。\n\n舞台側翼的暗影中，首席小提琴手身穿修身筆挺的黑色燕尾服，步履優雅地邁步走向聚光燈的焦點。\n\n他的臉色蒼白得近乎透明，鼻樑高挺，深陷的眼窩中跳動著兩簇幽冷得令人膽寒的火苗。在他左手握著的那把小提琴琴頭上，赫然鑲嵌著一隻散發著冰冷光澤的黃銅銜尾蛇卡榫。\n\n那是秦墨。\n\n「今晚，在正式演奏勃拉姆斯協奏曲之前，」秦墨走到麥克風前，聲音低沉優雅，帶著一股磁石般的奇異吸引力，「我謹將這首無伴奏引子，獻給三十年前沉睡在長江冰冷淤泥深處的啟蒙導師——林清源先生。」\n\n台下的楚天成聽到「林清源」三個字，臉上的笑容瞬間凝固成了一張慘白的死人面具。\n\n全場觀眾尚在面面相覷之時，秦墨手中的琴弓已凌空落下！\n\n「錚——！」\n\n那不是尋常羊腸線或尼龍弦發出的音色，而是一聲尖銳、冰冷、宛如手術刀劃破胸膜般的金屬撕裂聲！\n\n琴弓上的十三根弓毛，赫然是由高強度鈦鎳合金絲與人體骨膠原微纖維絞合而成。當琴弓擦過琴弦的剎那，整座大劇院的環繞立體聲擴音矩陣突然爆發出一陣低頻嘯叫！\n\n「唔！」\n\n第一排的楚天成突然痛苦地捂住了胸口，呼吸急促，臉色慘白如紙。\n\n後台入口處，裴以安與老周已疾步逼近舞台邊緣。裴以安盯著秦墨拉動琴弓的特殊指法，眼眸冷冽至極：「次聲波諧振。他的琴箱內部裝有高頻微型壓電發振器，琴弦震動引發的次聲波頻率正好是七點八三赫茲——人體心臟的固有機械共振頻率！他是要用聲波直接誘發楚天成的心室纖顫！」\n\n「楚天成有嚴重心肌缺血和冠心病病史，這不是暗殺，這是偽裝成心源性猝死的物理處決！」老周怒吼一聲，猛地掀開後台布幔，身手矯健得完全不像個五十歲的老刑警，如獵豹般撲向舞台！\n\n「住手！市局刑偵支隊！」老周震耳欲聾的怒吼在整個大劇院迴盪。\n\n全場觀眾瞬間一片大嘩！\n\n秦墨眼中閃過一絲冰冷的嘲諷，琴弓非但沒有停滯，反而以令人眼花繚亂的急速拉出了一連串如同狂風驟雨般的連頓弓！\n\n次聲波能量在空氣中激盪，楚天成雙眼翻白，整個人從包廂座椅上滑落，痛苦地在地上抽搐痙攣！\n\n就在琴弓即將劃出最後一道致命強音的千鈞一髮之際——\n\n「嗖！」\n\n一道銀色的流光撕裂空氣，精準無比地扎進了小提琴的共鳴箱面板！\n\n那是一柄純銀打造的十四號解剖手術刀！\n\n手術刀深深楔入琴箱的「F孔」邊緣，鋒利的刀刃直接切斷了底部的微型諧振晶振線路，狂暴的次聲波雜音在瞬間戛然而止！\n\n秦墨身形微晃，抬起眼眸，望向站在舞台側前方的裴以安。\n\n裴以安雙手插在工裝口袋裡，腳步不疾不徐地走上舞台，金絲眼鏡在聚光燈下反射著耀眼的寒芒：「秦墨，三十年前你從乾塢帶走林清源的頭骨，並不是為了復仇，而是為了保留證據。今天你如果在這裡殺了楚天成，死因只會是突發心梗，楚氏集團的黑幕將會隨著他的火化徹底湮滅。」\n\n「那你告訴我，法律給過我師父公道嗎？！」秦墨聲音嘶啞，三十年來壓抑的仇恨與痛苦如火山般自喉嚨深處爆發，「三十年了！兇手戴著勳章受人敬仰，而我師父的骨頭卻在下水道的爛泥裡泡了三十年！」\n\n「你的法醫鑒定還沒有做完。」裴以安神色冷靜而平靜，緩緩從風衣內側掏出一隻密封的無菌證物袋。\n\n袋子裡裝著的，正是剛剛從地下幹渠那具頭骨牙齒上拓印下來的顯微激光切片。\n\n「林清源的枕骨粉碎性骨折處，殘留著直徑一點二毫米的黃銅微粒，成分與楚天成三十年前擔任副院長時配發的特製純銅手術錘完全吻合。」裴以安的聲音清晰洪亮，透過舞台麥克風在整個大劇院上空炸響，「市局技術科已經同步扣押了楚天成保險庫裡的所有資產帳冊與三十年前的病理原始底稿。三十年前的真相，由活著的法醫送上法庭，而不是由你的私刑送進墳墓。」\n\n舞台下方，癱軟在地的楚天成聽到這句話，面如死灰，整個人徹底癱軟如爛泥。\n\n秦墨死死盯著裴以安手中的證物袋，握著琴弓的手指劇烈顫抖著，一行清淚終於從他凹陷的眼眶中無聲滑落。\n\n「啪嗒。」\n\n那把承載了三十年怨念的小提琴從他手中滑落，重重摔在光可鑑人的柚木舞台上。\n\n老周邁步上前，手銬清脆地扣上了秦墨的手腕。老刑警長長嘆了一口氣，伸手替秦墨整理了一下凌亂的燕尾服衣領：「小子……三十年了，跟老子回局裡，喝杯熱水吧。」\n\n秦墨仰起頭，看著頭頂璀璨如星海的劇院穹頂，嘴角泛起一抹釋然卻又無比詭異的微笑。\n\n「周警官，裴法醫……你們以為抓住我，這座城市的交響樂就結束了嗎？」\n\n秦墨的聲音輕若蚊蠅，卻讓裴以安的瞳孔狠狠收縮：\n\n「我只是個拉琴的學徒。真正的『擺渡人』……此時此刻，正坐在市局法醫中心的停屍房裡，等著你們帶我的骨頭回去呢。」\n\n舞台上方的遠處，老城區鐘樓沉悶悠遠的八點鐘聲，終於穿透漫天風雨，轟然敲響。\n\n【第二卷：雨夜骨骼交響曲 · 全卷完】","rawContentEn":"# Chapter 13: The Final Movement at the Grand Theatre\n\nAt 7:50 in the evening, barely ten minutes remained before the eight o'clock curtain chimes.\n\nAbove the rain-lashed expanse of the river, the Binjiang Grand Theatre resembled a colossal crystal seashell reclining across the stormy night, its soaring dome of tempered glass and titanium alloy trusses gleaming with an icy, blinding silver beneath flashes of lightning.\n\nOutside the grand portico, luxury sedans converged in droves as the city's high-society elite, civic dignitaries, and corporate magnates filed across rain-drenched red carpets. Meanwhile, deep in the gloom of the subterranean stormwater retention vault beneath the theatre, a rusted iron maintenance hatch was kicked open with a violent crash.\n\nOld Zhou emerged dripping with putrid, soot-black slurry, his trousers hitched above his knees, grimly shielding his pink thermos with its faded strawberry logo against his tactical vest while keeping his service pistol cocked in his right hand.\n\n\"Cough... hack! In thirty years of hunting killers and raiding smuggler dens, this is the very first time I've crawled through three kilometers of sewer pipe just to attend a high-brow symphony,\" Old Zhou grumbled, wiping rainwater from his eyes as he swept the service corridor leading backstage. \"Little Pei, looking like this, do you reckon the security guards will pin me against the wall with riot forks?\"\n\n\"From the perspectives of epidemiology and public sanitation, security would have ample justification to quarantine you and fumigate your entire vicinity,\" Pei Yi'an replied, dropping lithely from the ladder with his forensic kit, his trench coat mud-splattered yet his gaze behind gold-rimmed spectacles as dispassionate as a vernier caliper. \"Nine minutes until the clocktower strikes eight. The guest dressing room is the third door on the left.\"\n\nEvading patrol guards, the pair hurried along the carpeted, acoustically insulated backstage corridors.\n\nThe backstage area was a flurry of organized chaos: musicians clad in tailored tailcoats and sweeping evening gowns tuned their strings, applied rosin, and leafed through sheet music. The atmosphere hummed with the mingled aromas of turpentine, luxury perfume, and pre-performance adrenaline.\n\n\"Hold,\" Pei Yi'an halted suddenly, his eyes cutting like a scalpel through the ajar dressing room door.\n\nUpon the lounge sofa inside, the evening's guest concertmaster lay slumped in deep slumber before the vanity mirror, breathing rhythmically. Pei Yi'an stepped inside, rolled back an eyelid, and pressed two fingers against his carotid artery: \"Pupillary light reflex is sluggish, with faint traces of almond sweetness on the breath. An intravenous micro-dose of propofol—titrated with milligram precision to induce exactly three hours of sedation without risking respiratory depression.\"\n\nOn the brass valet stand beside the mirror, the tailor-made tailcoat was gone, along with the antique Guarneri violin from its velvet-lined case.\n\n\"He switched places! That brat put on the tailcoat and slipped into the orchestra pit!\" Old Zhou's expression darkened as he lunged toward the stage wings.\n\n\"Captain Zhou, hold your ground,\" Pei Yi'an seized Old Zhou's wrist with unexpected, iron grip. \"Eighteen hundred spectators occupy that auditorium, the front tiers lined with municipal leaders and chamber of commerce chairmen. If you charge in waving a sidearm and screaming about explosives, the resulting stampede will cause casualties far outstripping a targeted blast.\"\n\n\"Then what the hell do you propose I do? Stand by and watch him blow eighteen hundred innocent souls to kingdom come?!\" Old Zhou ground his molars, his eyes rimmed with blood.\n\n\"The microwave detonation link was severed and failsafe-locked in the aqueduct; he holds no remote trigger,\" Pei Yi'an pointed to the sodden invitation. \"The primary patron of tonight's gala is Chu Tiancheng, Chairman of Chu Bio-Pharmaceutical Corporation—the former vice-director of Municipal Hospital's pathology institute thirty years ago, and Dr. Lin Qingyuan's immediate supervisor.\"\n\nOld Zhou shuddered violently, all disparate puzzle pieces snapping together like an electric arc. \"Chu Tiancheng?! After Dr. Lin was murdered thirty years ago, he was the one who seized all of Lin's anti-cancer patents, founded Chu Bio-Pharmaceutical, and became the wealthiest tycoon in Binjiang!\"\n\n\"Lin Qingyuan's cranium bears comminuted blunt-force trauma, and Chu Tiancheng built his financial empire upon that bloodstained intellectual property,\" Pei Yi'an said, swiftly slipping into an attendant's dark stagehand coat and clipping on an ID pass. \"Qin Mo does not seek to slaughter the innocent. He intends, on the night of Chu Tiancheng's lifetime achievement commendation, to use Lin Qingyuan's bones to execute a death sentence thirty years overdue.\"\n\nOut front, the chime signaling the opening of the performance rang out clear and sharp.\n\n7:58 in the evening.\n\nThe glittering crystal chandeliers in the Grand Theatre's primary auditorium dimmed in slow unison as azure spotlights cascaded like liquid silver upon center stage. Thunderous applause erupted from the eighteen hundred patrons in attendance.\n\nIn the center box of the front row, sixty-something Chu Tiancheng, his silver hair groomed to absolute perfection, straightened the glistening \"Civic Medal of Distinguished Contribution\" pinned to his lapel, beaming as he nodded to surrounding dignitaries and socialites.\n\nFrom the shadowed wings, the guest concertmaster, dressed in a sharply tailored black tailcoat, strode with poised grace into the focus of the spotlights.\n\nHis complexion was pale to the point of translucence, his nose aquiline, and deep within his hollow sockets burned two chilling pinpricks of cold flame. Clutched in his left hand was a violin whose scroll was capped with a gleaming brass ouroboros slide.\n\nIt was Qin Mo.\n\n\"Tonight, prior to commencing Brahms' Concerto,\" Qin Mo addressed the standing microphone, his voice cultured, resonant, and possessing an almost hypnotic cadence, \"I take the liberty of dedicating this unscripted solo introduction to my mentor, who has slept for thirty years in the freezing silt of the Yangtze River—Dr. Lin Qingyuan.\"\n\nHearing the name \"Lin Qingyuan,\" the triumphant grin on Chu Tiancheng's face froze in an instant into a ghastly, bloodless death mask.\n\nWhile the audience exchanged puzzled whispers, the bow in Qin Mo's right hand descended through the air!\n\n*Skrrrt—!*\n\nIt was no tone of gut or nylon, but a piercing, metallic shriek resembling a scalpel slicing through visceral pleura!\n\nThe thirteen filaments strung across the bow were braided from high-tensile nickel-titanium wire and human collagen fibrils. The moment hair bit string, the surround-sound matrix throughout the theatre wailed with a violent sub-bass howl!\n\n\"Ugh!\"\n\nIn the front row, Chu Tiancheng clutched his chest in sudden agony, gasping for air as all color drained from his face.\n\nAt the edge of the proscenium, Pei Yi'an and Old Zhou closed in. Pei Yi'an's eyes narrowed on Qin Mo's fingerings: \"Infrasonic resonance. The violin body houses a miniature piezoelectric transducer; the sub-harmonic frequency generated by the strings sits at precisely 7.83 Hertz—the intrinsic mechanical resonant frequency of the human myocardium! He is utilizing acoustic resonance to trigger ventricular fibrillation!\"\n\n\"Chu Tiancheng has a clinical history of myocardial ischemia and coronary disease—this isn't mere assassination, it's an acoustic execution engineered to masquerade as natural cardiac arrest!\" Old Zhou roared, tearing aside the stage curtains and lunging forward with the agility of a panther!\n\n\"Police! Freeze! Municipal Criminal Investigation Detachment!\" Old Zhou's thunderous shout echoed through the cavernous hall.\n\nThe entire auditorium erupted into instant pandemonium!\n\nA sneer of cold disdain flickered across Qin Mo's eyes; rather than halting, his wrist flicked into a breathtaking staccato flurry like a raging tempest!\n\nShockwaves of infrasound pulsated through the air. Chu Tiancheng's eyes rolled upward as he slipped from his seat, convulsing violently upon the carpeted floor!\n\nJust as the bow hovered to strike the fatal crescendo—\n\n*Whoosh!*\n\nA streak of silver sliced the air, biting into the violin's spruce soundboard with uncanny precision!\n\nIt was a solid-silver No. 14 dissecting scalpel!\n\nThe blade embedded deep into the lip of the treble f-hole, severing the crystal oscillator circuit beneath; in a split second, the demonic hum collapsed into dead silence!\n\nQin Mo swayed slightly, raising his gaze toward Pei Yi'an standing at the apron of the stage.\n\nHands tucked into his coat pockets, Pei Yi'an stepped unhurriedly into the glare of the spotlights, his glasses catching the brilliant white glare: \"Qin Mo, when you removed Lin Qingyuan's cranium thirty years ago, your purpose was not revenge, but preservation of evidence. If you slay Chu Tiancheng tonight, his death will be ruled acute myocardial infarction, and the atrocities of the Chu Corporation will be cremated alongside his corpse.\"\n\n\"Then tell me, did the law ever grant my master justice?!\" Qin Mo rasped, three decades of suppressed fury and agony erupting from his throat like volcanic lava. \"Thirty years! The killer basks in honors and medals, while my mentor's bones soaked in the sewer sludge for thirty years!\"\n\n\"Your forensic post-mortem was never completed,\" Pei Yi'an said with tranquil calm, withdrawing a sealed, sterile evidence pouch from within his lapel.\n\nSealed inside was the micro-laser polarized imprint just harvested from the cranium's dentition in the aqueduct.\n\n\"Embedded within Lin Qingyuan's occipital fracture are 1.2-millimeter brass particulate residues, chemically identical to the custom brass mallet issued to Chu Tiancheng when he served as vice-director thirty years ago,\" Pei Yi'an's voice resonated clearly through the microphone across the hall. \"The Criminalistics Division has simultaneously impounded Chu Tiancheng's vault ledgers and the original 1994 pathology manuscripts. The truth of thirty years ago shall be carried into a court of law by living forensic scientists—not buried in a grave by your vigilante executions.\"\n\nDown in the stalls, Chu Tiancheng slumped upon the floor, ashen-faced and limp as wet clay upon hearing those words.\n\nQin Mo stared fixedly at the evidence pouch, his fingers trembling upon the bow until a solitary tear spilled silently down his hollow cheek.\n\n*Clatter.*\n\nThe violin bearing three decades of torment slipped from his grasp, striking the polished teak boards with a hollow echo.\n\nOld Zhou stepped forward, the handcuffs snapping crisply around Qin Mo's wrists. The veteran detective exhaled a heavy sigh, gently adjusting the rumpled collar of Qin Mo's tailcoat: \"Kid... it's been thirty years. Come back to the station with me and drink a cup of hot water.\"\n\nTilting his head back toward the sea of glittering lights in the dome, Qin Mo's lips curved into an expression of relief—tinged with an eerie, knowing smile.\n\n\"Captain Zhou, Doctor Pei... do you truly believe that by apprehending me, this city's symphony has reached its finale?\"\n\nQin Mo's whisper was barely audible, yet it sent a sharp jolt through Pei Yi'an's pupils:\n\n\"I was merely an apprentice bowing the strings. The true 'Ferryman'... at this very moment, sits within the morgue of your own Forensic Center, waiting for you to return with my bones.\"\n\nIn the distance above the stage, the deep, solemn chime of eight o'clock from the historic clocktower finally boomed through the driving rain.\n\n[Volume Two: Rain-Night Bone Symphony · End of Volume]"}];
